1
00:02:16,411 --> 00:02:20,147
(After Benjamin's eviction)

2
00:02:28,490 --> 00:02:30,090
Goodbye, everyone. I hope you all fail.

3
00:02:30,492 --> 00:02:31,792
Goodness.

4
00:02:36,298 --> 00:02:37,231
But why...

5
00:02:37,232 --> 00:02:39,334
I might just be being too emotional,

6
00:02:39,335 --> 00:02:40,868
- but why do I feel awful?
- Of course.

7
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:42,236
Weren't you here...

8
00:02:42,237 --> 00:02:43,437
when he called us "dyscalculics" again?

9
00:02:43,905 --> 00:02:45,606
So Gray swore.

10
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:49,343
Oh, my.

11
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:50,878
It was all lies.

12
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,113
- And he made them all believable.
- Earlier, he said...

13
00:02:53,114 --> 00:02:54,448
how he was going back and forth...

14
00:02:54,449 --> 00:02:56,618
because of his work visa.

15
00:02:56,619 --> 00:02:58,452
- Right!
- He gave us a long story...

16
00:02:58,453 --> 00:03:00,287
about how he went to Goyang
Foreign Language High School for a bit.

17
00:03:00,523 --> 00:03:02,623
What was I even listening to?

18
00:03:02,624 --> 00:03:03,791
He's a genius, though.

19
00:03:04,493 --> 00:03:05,793
He had a lot of fun...

20
00:03:05,794 --> 00:03:07,662
making up this story.

21
00:03:08,163 --> 00:03:08,996
I'm shocked.

22
00:03:11,033 --> 00:03:12,834
(Michael didn't receive any prize money
after the Life Speeches.)

23
00:03:12,835 --> 00:03:13,901
I...

24
00:03:16,171 --> 00:03:17,872
I'm a little ticked off now.

25
00:03:17,873 --> 00:03:19,607
- I'm furious.
- Right.

26
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,142
This is...

27
00:03:21,343 --> 00:03:24,278
I worked so hard...

28
00:03:24,279 --> 00:03:25,713
to track down the spy.

29
00:03:25,714 --> 00:03:27,014
I almost even got eliminated.

30
00:03:27,616 --> 00:03:29,884
I'm sorry. I didn't think about that...

31
00:03:29,885 --> 00:03:32,186
because the second round was a free vote.

32
00:03:32,187 --> 00:03:33,154
I know.

33
00:03:33,623 --> 00:03:36,457
I didn't want to beg for hearts either.

34
00:03:36,458 --> 00:03:38,092
I don't really feel good...

35
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:39,661
about the whole situation.

36
00:03:39,662 --> 00:03:43,564
They keep calling it a community,
but it's nothing more than a name.

37
00:03:46,568 --> 00:03:48,802
I feel like I have to bring this up.

38
00:03:48,803 --> 00:03:52,239
Michael is a little upset...

39
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:53,407
- because...
- Why?

40
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,977
His balance came down to zero...

41
00:03:55,978 --> 00:03:57,311
because the spy attacked him.

42
00:03:57,312 --> 00:03:58,479
And...

43
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:01,682
since Round Two was a free vote,

44
00:04:01,863 --> 00:04:03,630
he doesn't have much money right now.

45
00:04:04,586 --> 00:04:06,320
He needed some help with that,
but we overlooked it.

46
00:04:06,321 --> 00:04:09,023
I don't really want to beg.

47
00:04:09,658 --> 00:04:12,693
- I just hope you guys understand.
- I'm sorry about that.

48
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,829
Why don't we get him a pack
of cigarettes to cheer him up?

49
00:04:15,830 --> 00:04:18,665
Right. I think that's called for.

50
00:04:19,167 --> 00:04:20,400
Are you trying to make up for it
with cigarettes?

51
00:04:20,401 --> 00:04:21,301
- No.
- No.

52
00:04:21,770 --> 00:04:22,670
I'm kidding.

53
00:04:24,439 --> 00:04:26,240
I'll charge ten percent.

54
00:04:26,608 --> 00:04:27,775
(Community fund: 14,397.03 dollars)

55
00:04:27,776 --> 00:04:31,545
(Community fund: 23,251 dollars)

56
00:04:31,546 --> 00:04:34,415
We'll have seven sets
of fried chicken and beer,

57
00:04:34,416 --> 00:04:36,850
two bottles of soju, two cartons of milk,
and one pack of cigarettes.

58
00:04:36,851 --> 00:04:37,985
(Community Mart Dinner: 5,200 dollars)

59
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:40,287
- Your purchase has been completed.
- Still, we have more than 10,000 dollars.

60
00:04:40,288 --> 00:04:41,623
It'll be deducted from the community fund.

61
00:04:42,224 --> 00:04:44,292
- I'll go get some fresh air.
- Let's go.

62
00:04:45,527 --> 00:04:48,162
What disappointed me most was...

63
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:50,764
I'm really disappointed in Genie.

64
00:04:51,433 --> 00:04:53,567
She cried because she couldn't eat
Peking duck.

65
00:04:53,735 --> 00:04:55,135
- I know.
- And she...

66
00:04:55,237 --> 00:04:56,906
desperately wants to win here.

67
00:04:56,907 --> 00:04:58,472
She's so hungry for victory.

68
00:04:58,473 --> 00:05:01,509
I can see how hypocritical she is.

69
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:04,312
I'm going to root out hypocrites
from now on.

70
00:05:04,313 --> 00:05:05,279
Hypocrites.

71
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:08,449
Also, why was the spy so arrogant?

72
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,318
You guys don't want to do well.

73
00:05:10,319 --> 00:05:11,919
You dyscalculics.

74
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,287
Goodbye, everyone. I hope you all fail.

75
00:05:13,421 --> 00:05:16,723
I didn't like how he talked down
to us like we were some morons...

76
00:05:16,724 --> 00:05:17,724
when he left.

77
00:05:18,126 --> 00:05:21,161
He was so arrogant. Zero humility.

78
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:23,864
- Ace, cheer up!
- Thanks.

79
00:05:24,332 --> 00:05:25,432
I'm looking out for you.

80
00:05:25,567 --> 00:05:27,034
Thank you, Dark Knight.

81
00:05:27,903 --> 00:05:29,337
Superman, have a seat.

82
00:05:30,272 --> 00:05:31,273
Help him.

83
00:05:31,907 --> 00:05:33,608
- How can I help?
- Any way you can.

84
00:05:34,342 --> 00:05:35,208
Okay.

85
00:05:36,578 --> 00:05:37,378
Superman.

86
00:05:37,379 --> 00:05:38,812
(During the Lifetime Leader vote)

87
00:05:38,813 --> 00:05:43,884
(Dark Knight was the only person
who voted for Superman.)

88
00:05:44,186 --> 00:05:46,487
You know me. I'm all about loyalty.

89
00:05:46,621 --> 00:05:48,755
You guys were the only people...

90
00:05:48,756 --> 00:05:50,658
I turned to for help from Day One.

91
00:05:50,659 --> 00:05:52,793
You know I've been looking out
for Michael...

92
00:05:53,295 --> 00:05:54,795
and you as well.

93
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:56,830
I was the only one who gave you
a helping hand...

94
00:05:56,831 --> 00:05:58,065
when you needed it.

95
00:05:58,433 --> 00:05:59,566
Keep that in mind.

96
00:06:02,804 --> 00:06:05,406
Your order has arrived.

97
00:06:05,974 --> 00:06:08,809
I'm so happy. It looks good!

98
00:06:09,045 --> 00:06:12,279
Finally, we've eradicated the spy.

99
00:06:14,883 --> 00:06:16,584
Great job!

100
00:06:16,585 --> 00:06:18,986
- It's all thanks to Michael.
- Michael played a big role.

101
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,189
Now that we've beaten the final boss,

102
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,990
I don't know how to play the game anymore.

103
00:06:23,191 --> 00:06:24,691
I know. We got the boss.

104
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,261
And yet, the end credits aren't rolling.

105
00:06:29,164 --> 00:06:30,465
(The announcement will now begin.)

106
00:06:30,466 --> 00:06:33,634
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

107
00:06:33,635 --> 00:06:34,435
What?

108
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:40,774
We have an evictee today.

109
00:06:41,377 --> 00:06:46,047
Today's evictee is Benjamin.

110
00:06:48,283 --> 00:06:51,452
Benjamin...

111
00:06:53,355 --> 00:06:55,088
was the spy.

112
00:06:57,059 --> 00:06:59,359
Since the spy was evicted,

113
00:07:01,263 --> 00:07:04,031
a new spy was appointed.

114
00:07:10,639 --> 00:07:11,606
So, that was true?

115
00:07:13,208 --> 00:07:15,142
- For real?
- So, what he said was true.

116
00:07:15,511 --> 00:07:18,178
When Benjamin was talking about it,

117
00:07:18,179 --> 00:07:20,681
it went in one ear and out the other.

118
00:07:20,682 --> 00:07:22,849
Once I found out
that a new spy was appointed,

119
00:07:22,850 --> 00:07:24,885
I had no idea what to do.

120
00:07:25,854 --> 00:07:28,556
I'd completely let my guard down.

121
00:07:28,557 --> 00:07:31,626
I wonder what moves the new spy will make.

122
00:07:31,627 --> 00:07:32,760
I'm really curious to see.

123
00:07:34,656 --> 00:07:36,430
Who is the new spy?

124
00:07:36,431 --> 00:07:38,899
This is so tough.

125
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:43,103
I don't think
they'd be 100 percent sure it's me.

126
00:07:43,305 --> 00:07:45,773
I'm picturing myself coming out on top
by turning their distrust...

127
00:07:45,774 --> 00:07:47,675
against each other.

128
00:07:50,812 --> 00:07:52,112
(Tensions Under the Roof)

129
00:07:52,414 --> 00:07:54,382
(The Community)

130
00:07:55,150 --> 00:07:58,719
(Start the Dilemma Game)

131
00:08:00,622 --> 00:08:01,989
Now,

132
00:08:02,157 --> 00:08:05,058
we will have the final favorability vote.

133
00:08:07,095 --> 00:08:09,397
Here are the rules...

134
00:08:09,398 --> 00:08:11,017
- for the final favorability vote.
- Michael, remember our deal!

135
00:08:11,018 --> 00:08:11,865
Okay!

136
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:15,135
You have 90 minutes...

137
00:08:15,637 --> 00:08:18,338
to cast your final favorability vote.

138
00:08:19,574 --> 00:08:21,241
Once voting closes...

139
00:08:21,242 --> 00:08:23,944
"The two residents with the lowest
cumulative favorability scores..."

140
00:08:23,945 --> 00:08:25,712
"will be immediately evicted." Two people.

141
00:08:26,181 --> 00:08:27,148
Two?

142
00:08:32,654 --> 00:08:37,858
(Current Favorability Vote Ranking)

143
00:08:37,859 --> 00:08:39,693
(Current eviction candidates)

144
00:08:39,694 --> 00:08:43,430
However, the Lifetime Leader cannot be
an eviction candidate.

145
00:08:43,431 --> 00:08:44,265
(Excluded)

146
00:08:44,433 --> 00:08:47,067
If two residents have
the same favorability score,

147
00:08:47,436 --> 00:08:52,206
the resident with more personal funds
ranks higher.

148
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:56,376
Each resident receives one vote.

149
00:08:57,712 --> 00:09:00,080
"You may vote for yourself."

150
00:09:00,781 --> 00:09:03,116
- Then we should vote for ourselves.
- I guess that's what everyone will do.

151
00:09:03,117 --> 00:09:04,618
We should vote for ourselves.

152
00:09:05,354 --> 00:09:07,521
For the final favorability vote,

153
00:09:07,789 --> 00:09:10,892
additional votes can be purchased...

154
00:09:10,893 --> 00:09:12,860
at the Community Center with no limit.

155
00:09:12,861 --> 00:09:14,762
"Each additional vote costs..."

156
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:17,798
"exactly 1,000 dollars in personal funds."

157
00:09:19,601 --> 00:09:22,502
If you want to survive,
you should keep spending money.

158
00:09:22,503 --> 00:09:24,804
You should spend money
to vote for yourself.

159
00:09:24,805 --> 00:09:26,739
They're making us drain our funds.

160
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:29,042
You'd be spending 10,000 dollars
to buy 10 votes.

161
00:09:29,344 --> 00:09:30,244
I know.

162
00:09:30,245 --> 00:09:33,013
Is this really worth the opportunity cost?

163
00:09:33,782 --> 00:09:36,384
If you hold an immunity card,

164
00:09:36,385 --> 00:09:37,818
you will not be evicted.

165
00:09:37,819 --> 00:09:40,154
"The Community Center will close..."

166
00:09:40,155 --> 00:09:41,756
"twenty minutes after voting ends."

167
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:47,060
If you want to transfer
your immunity card,

168
00:09:47,061 --> 00:09:49,763
you'll have 20 minutes
after that countdown ends.

169
00:09:49,764 --> 00:09:50,897
About 20 minutes.

170
00:09:50,898 --> 00:09:52,666
(The only person with immunity: Genie)

171
00:09:56,604 --> 00:09:59,573
We could've checked this information
if the Reporter survived.

172
00:10:02,044 --> 00:10:04,745
The final favorability vote
will now begin...

173
00:10:04,912 --> 00:10:07,581
and be open for 90 minutes.

174
00:10:08,917 --> 00:10:10,651
I did think it was a crisis.

175
00:10:10,652 --> 00:10:12,820
I was sure my score was above average,

176
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:15,590
but I also thought some people
would buy more votes.

177
00:10:15,591 --> 00:10:17,391
I was a little anxious.

178
00:10:17,825 --> 00:10:20,961
I realized that the favorability vote was
important enough...

179
00:10:20,962 --> 00:10:22,596
to determine the final eliminations.

180
00:10:22,830 --> 00:10:26,266
I didn't think I did too badly
with the hearts,

181
00:10:26,434 --> 00:10:28,536
so I thought I'd be okay.

182
00:10:28,537 --> 00:10:30,504
I thought it'd be a fun game of chicken.

183
00:10:30,505 --> 00:10:33,707
If I found out someone spent a ton
of money, I'd want to spend more too.

184
00:10:33,708 --> 00:10:37,677
It'd come down to how much
we'd be willing to shell out.

185
00:10:38,013 --> 00:10:40,213
If you'd like to vote,

186
00:10:40,682 --> 00:10:43,584
please visit the Community Center.

187
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,786
I'll go vote.

188
00:10:49,124 --> 00:10:50,057
Okay.

189
00:10:50,625 --> 00:10:53,560
Don't overthink this. Be cool.

190
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,107
(Dark Knight)

191
00:11:07,775 --> 00:11:08,708
Here's my vote.

192
00:11:09,277 --> 00:11:10,777
(Dark Knight: 6,076 dollars, 19 votes)

193
00:11:10,778 --> 00:11:13,046
(Dark Knight: 6,076.23 dollars, 20 votes)

194
00:11:13,215 --> 00:11:14,514
I'll buy six extra ballots.

195
00:11:15,450 --> 00:11:16,750
(Your funds have been reduced
by 6,000 dollars.)

196
00:11:16,751 --> 00:11:18,285
(Dark Knight: 76 dollars, 20 votes)

197
00:11:18,286 --> 00:11:19,586
I'm flat broke now.

198
00:11:20,455 --> 00:11:25,193
(Dark Knight)

199
00:11:25,194 --> 00:11:26,660
Done!

200
00:11:27,330 --> 00:11:29,196
This is just life.

201
00:11:29,197 --> 00:11:30,431
(Dark Knight: 76 dollars, 26 votes)

202
00:11:30,432 --> 00:11:31,965
I went all in.

203
00:11:32,033 --> 00:11:35,835
I think surviving is worth
more than the money.

204
00:11:41,109 --> 00:11:42,810
Do you want me to buy you some?

205
00:11:42,844 --> 00:11:43,844
I'd really appreciate it.

206
00:11:43,845 --> 00:11:45,779
I have 22 now.

207
00:11:46,681 --> 00:11:47,814
I have 16.

208
00:11:48,717 --> 00:11:50,484
I'm most likely to be evicted.

209
00:11:50,485 --> 00:11:53,521
I think I can buy you some votes.

210
00:11:53,522 --> 00:11:54,521
Is that so?

211
00:11:54,989 --> 00:11:57,958
I had a good reason to keep Michael alive.

212
00:11:57,959 --> 00:12:00,661
Since he was sure...

213
00:12:00,662 --> 00:12:02,195
I wasn't the spy,

214
00:12:02,196 --> 00:12:05,432
I was calculating how many votes
I'd need to win him over.

215
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:10,170
I tried to get others on board.

216
00:12:10,572 --> 00:12:11,672
Did you vote?

217
00:12:12,273 --> 00:12:14,240
I did.

218
00:12:14,241 --> 00:12:15,275
How many votes do you have?

219
00:12:15,677 --> 00:12:17,978
I brought my total to 20.

220
00:12:18,213 --> 00:12:19,147
Twenty?

221
00:12:19,148 --> 00:12:20,514
I brought it to 20.

222
00:12:20,515 --> 00:12:22,049
I figured it'd be safer.

223
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:24,218
He has 16, so even if he buys 1 more,

224
00:12:24,219 --> 00:12:25,686
he'll only have 17.

225
00:12:25,687 --> 00:12:28,522
Everyone here just needs to help me.

226
00:12:28,689 --> 00:12:30,891
Wait. You should help him.

227
00:12:30,892 --> 00:12:31,858
I'll help you.

228
00:12:32,128 --> 00:12:34,028
I told him I would.
That's why I pulled you aside.

229
00:12:34,562 --> 00:12:36,630
How many do you want me to get you?

230
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:38,331
Since he has 20,
should I bring yours to 20 too?

231
00:12:38,332 --> 00:12:39,533
That should be enough.

232
00:12:39,534 --> 00:12:40,467
Then...

233
00:12:40,468 --> 00:12:43,236
Hold on. Come over here.

234
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:44,971
I know...

235
00:12:45,673 --> 00:12:48,208
I said 20,
but you shouldn't just make it 20.

236
00:12:48,209 --> 00:12:49,042
- Why?
- Why?

237
00:12:49,043 --> 00:12:50,710
- I'll be honest.
- Okay.

238
00:12:50,711 --> 00:12:54,114
I had about 6,400 dollars left.

239
00:12:54,282 --> 00:12:55,716
I just spent it all.

240
00:12:55,717 --> 00:12:57,150
So how many do you have now?

241
00:12:57,151 --> 00:12:59,286
Twenty... Hang on.

242
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,521
I bought 6, so I have 18 now.

243
00:13:01,522 --> 00:13:02,422
Twenty-four.

244
00:13:03,291 --> 00:13:05,091
I brought it to 24.

245
00:13:05,092 --> 00:13:06,126
So, Gray...

246
00:13:06,127 --> 00:13:07,494
I'll buy him some.

247
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:09,663
Three should be enough.

248
00:13:09,664 --> 00:13:12,666
I'll buy you three votes.

249
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,301
By the way, Gray, please.

250
00:13:14,302 --> 00:13:16,202
- Please don't tell people.
- I won't.

251
00:13:16,203 --> 00:13:17,437
I know you're sly.

252
00:13:17,438 --> 00:13:19,139
You guys say I'm sly,

253
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:20,874
but honestly, I've never repeated...

254
00:13:20,875 --> 00:13:22,442
what I heard.

255
00:13:22,443 --> 00:13:24,010
I was just joking,

256
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:26,713
but please keep this between us.
I put everything I had into this.

257
00:13:26,714 --> 00:13:28,182
Hey, I want to talk to him first.

258
00:13:28,183 --> 00:13:30,050
Look. I could've lied,

259
00:13:30,051 --> 00:13:32,686
but since I'm honest,
I told you the truth.

260
00:13:33,154 --> 00:13:34,087
Right?

261
00:13:35,757 --> 00:13:36,924
With this...

262
00:13:37,692 --> 00:13:40,194
I don't see how I can help you.

263
00:13:40,661 --> 00:13:42,796
You should give me your vote.

264
00:13:42,797 --> 00:13:44,531
We only get one ballot.

265
00:13:45,166 --> 00:13:46,032
Superman.

266
00:13:46,768 --> 00:13:47,768
Just give me one vote.

267
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:49,870
Can I buy more ballots?

268
00:13:49,871 --> 00:13:52,740
- No. You should be getting one.
- Right?

269
00:13:55,077 --> 00:13:56,810
He's way behind in votes.

270
00:13:57,312 --> 00:13:58,245
I have 16.

271
00:13:59,314 --> 00:14:00,881
Let's cut to the chase.

272
00:14:00,882 --> 00:14:02,383
Let's do this. Wait.

273
00:14:02,384 --> 00:14:05,185
Anyway, just give me one vote.

274
00:14:05,186 --> 00:14:07,321
- Put one vote on me.
- One favorability vote?

275
00:14:07,322 --> 00:14:09,056
Give me one favorability vote.

276
00:14:09,057 --> 00:14:10,124
One vote.

277
00:14:10,658 --> 00:14:12,959
- I told you I'd help you.
- Yes.

278
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,495
He has a lot. He said he has 26.

279
00:14:15,496 --> 00:14:16,863
- Dark Knight?
- Yes.

280
00:14:16,864 --> 00:14:18,398
Then he has even more than me.

281
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:20,266
Don't tell him I told you this.

282
00:14:22,036 --> 00:14:24,170
Can I have your attention?

283
00:14:24,972 --> 00:14:25,805
Excuse me.

284
00:14:27,185 --> 00:14:29,118
I just wanted...

285
00:14:29,143 --> 00:14:31,445
to look out for Michael
after everything he's done.

286
00:14:31,446 --> 00:14:33,947
I'm going to give him one vote.

287
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:36,484
I'm just going to put this out there...

288
00:14:36,485 --> 00:14:38,085
and leave you guys to think about it.

289
00:14:38,086 --> 00:14:39,920
He's done a lot for us,

290
00:14:39,921 --> 00:14:41,421
- I agree.
- but he doesn't like to burden people,

291
00:14:41,923 --> 00:14:43,924
so I'm speaking up for him.

292
00:14:43,925 --> 00:14:45,325
So,

293
00:14:45,326 --> 00:14:47,427
we're all going to vote for ourselves,

294
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:49,963
which won't change our current ranking.

295
00:14:49,964 --> 00:14:51,966
If we all vote for Michael,

296
00:14:51,967 --> 00:14:54,635
we'll be agreeing to save Michael.

297
00:14:54,636 --> 00:14:57,371
It's not whether we should save him
or not.

298
00:14:57,372 --> 00:14:59,506
- He's anxious right now.
- The ranking wouldn't change.

299
00:14:59,507 --> 00:15:02,141
I just want to give him recognition...

300
00:15:02,142 --> 00:15:04,177
for all the work he's done.

301
00:15:04,178 --> 00:15:07,380
I'm just saying I'm on board.

302
00:15:07,381 --> 00:15:09,883
I'm just trying to show some loyalty.

303
00:15:09,884 --> 00:15:12,852
Please think about what I said.

304
00:15:13,321 --> 00:15:15,922
I might've overstepped here.

305
00:15:15,923 --> 00:15:18,558
- Please.
- Ultimately, it's a personal choice.

306
00:15:24,565 --> 00:15:26,666
- There you go.
- Thanks, Dark Knight.

307
00:15:26,934 --> 00:15:29,335
We don't have to vote for Dark Knight.

308
00:15:29,604 --> 00:15:32,539
Are you actually going to spend
your own money to vote for them?

309
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:33,440
I...

310
00:15:33,441 --> 00:15:34,975
Is it really worth it?

311
00:15:34,976 --> 00:15:36,977
He only has 16.
Do we let him get eliminated?

312
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:39,212
This might end up becoming an arms race.

313
00:15:39,881 --> 00:15:41,048
We have to keep that in mind.

314
00:15:41,950 --> 00:15:44,284
If we put all our money into this,

315
00:15:45,019 --> 00:15:46,153
we'll have nothing to take home tomorrow.

316
00:15:46,154 --> 00:15:49,122
So we survive today,
only to have nothing left tomorrow?

317
00:15:49,123 --> 00:15:51,191
I know.
The prize money won't be that much.

318
00:15:51,192 --> 00:15:53,060
Assume everyone got
an equal share of hearts...

319
00:15:53,061 --> 00:15:55,562
and calculate how much each person
would have gotten per day.

320
00:15:55,563 --> 00:15:56,930
That's how we find the average.

321
00:15:56,931 --> 00:15:58,165
What's your average, then?

322
00:15:58,166 --> 00:16:00,200
That's why I said 19 or 20.

323
00:16:06,474 --> 00:16:07,808
How many hearts do you have?

324
00:16:08,176 --> 00:16:09,376
Sixteen.

325
00:16:09,811 --> 00:16:13,613
Then I'll buy you a heart.

326
00:16:13,614 --> 00:16:16,082
- Thank you.
- I think I have enough.

327
00:16:16,083 --> 00:16:18,285
- You have a lot, right?
- Twenty-four.

328
00:16:18,286 --> 00:16:19,919
You're good at those things.

329
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:21,888
(Sugar: 5,196 dollars, 24 votes)

330
00:16:22,757 --> 00:16:23,924
What happened?

331
00:16:23,925 --> 00:16:25,792
- How many hearts do you have now?
- Sixteen.

332
00:16:26,294 --> 00:16:28,161
I think you're on the higher side.

333
00:16:28,162 --> 00:16:29,998
- She is.
- Yes. I have 24.

334
00:16:29,999 --> 00:16:31,064
I'm so jealous.

335
00:16:31,065 --> 00:16:32,966
I'm going to give him a heart.

336
00:16:33,301 --> 00:16:36,403
Gray said he'd give me about three.

337
00:16:36,404 --> 00:16:38,005
Can you really trust him, though?

338
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:40,598
That'd cost 3,000 dollars.
That's real money.

339
00:16:41,409 --> 00:16:43,076
I'm the most likely to get eliminated.

340
00:16:43,077 --> 00:16:45,212
If I won first place for the Life Speech,

341
00:16:45,213 --> 00:16:46,646
I'd have 5,000 dollars.

342
00:16:46,647 --> 00:16:49,015
I wouldn't have to beg
and could just buy votes for myself.

343
00:16:49,016 --> 00:16:51,017
But I had no choice...

344
00:16:51,018 --> 00:16:53,553
but to swallow my pride
and ask people for help.

345
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:56,756
I felt bad, and it was really stressful.

346
00:17:00,214 --> 00:17:01,181
Hello.

347
00:17:02,430 --> 00:17:05,265
I'll vote for myself and buy one ballot...

348
00:17:05,266 --> 00:17:06,533
with 1,000 dollars.

349
00:17:08,503 --> 00:17:09,470
(Michael)

350
00:17:09,471 --> 00:17:11,138
(Michael: 620 dollars)

351
00:17:11,139 --> 00:17:12,005
(1,000 dollars deducted)

352
00:17:12,006 --> 00:17:12,873
(Michael: 620 dollars, 18 votes)

353
00:17:12,874 --> 00:17:14,541
(Two votes added)

354
00:17:15,009 --> 00:17:16,776
He's way behind in votes.

355
00:17:16,777 --> 00:17:17,744
I have 16.

356
00:17:18,279 --> 00:17:23,183
(Michael lied about only having 16 votes.)

357
00:17:23,951 --> 00:17:28,121
(Michael: 620 dollars, 20 votes)

358
00:17:28,256 --> 00:17:30,857
Guys, I have 24.

359
00:17:30,858 --> 00:17:32,359
I don't have to buy more, right?

360
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:34,361
I don't think you do.

361
00:17:34,362 --> 00:17:36,063
You're so safe.

362
00:17:36,297 --> 00:17:37,664
I think we have
around the same number of hearts.

363
00:17:37,665 --> 00:17:39,766
I don't have that many.

364
00:17:39,967 --> 00:17:41,267
How many do you have?

365
00:17:41,536 --> 00:17:43,704
I poured in all my money,
but I'm still in the low 20s.

366
00:17:43,705 --> 00:17:44,738
That's all I'm going to say.

367
00:17:44,739 --> 00:17:45,939
You know I don't lie.

368
00:17:46,073 --> 00:17:48,174
(Dark Knight: 76 dollars, 26 votes)

369
00:17:48,175 --> 00:17:50,209
I'm not sure how many I should buy.

370
00:17:50,210 --> 00:17:53,279
If you want to buy some,
three should be enough for you.

371
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,714
Should I buy 4 and make it 30?

372
00:17:54,849 --> 00:17:56,183
You have 26?

373
00:17:56,184 --> 00:17:59,386
- You made 5,000 dollars today.
- You have 26? Awesome.

374
00:17:59,387 --> 00:18:00,487
Do you really have 21?

375
00:18:01,188 --> 00:18:02,822
If that's true, don't buy too many.

376
00:18:02,823 --> 00:18:05,892
Even at most, everyone would be
in the high teens or low 20s.

377
00:18:06,226 --> 00:18:08,628
- So, how many does Michael have now?
- Look.

378
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:11,131
I'll give him 1, so that's 17.

379
00:18:11,132 --> 00:18:12,832
Dark Knight will give him 1,
so that makes it 18.

380
00:18:12,833 --> 00:18:15,701
He voted for himself, so that's 19.

381
00:18:15,702 --> 00:18:17,770
Are you sure Dark Knight bought him one?

382
00:18:18,439 --> 00:18:20,106
I think he said he would.

383
00:18:20,107 --> 00:18:21,775
But he already voted,

384
00:18:21,776 --> 00:18:24,177
and he said he spent all his money.

385
00:18:24,178 --> 00:18:26,279
- Is that so?
- Don't tell anyone.

386
00:18:29,417 --> 00:18:31,017
Dark Knight keeps lying.

387
00:18:31,018 --> 00:18:34,054
He said he didn't give him a vote.

388
00:18:34,055 --> 00:18:36,423
He talked to Sugar
like he'd given you one.

389
00:18:36,424 --> 00:18:37,758
He didn't.

390
00:18:37,759 --> 00:18:40,293
- Why did he do that?
- That's a bit strange.

391
00:18:40,294 --> 00:18:41,328
Is he the spy?

392
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,433
What did you and Gray talk about?

393
00:18:47,434 --> 00:18:49,335
About how many hearts we have.

394
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:51,871
Gray is not trustworthy.

395
00:18:51,872 --> 00:18:53,539
He's shady.

396
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:54,607
Don't trust him.

397
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:04,784
I'll buy five in total.

398
00:19:05,052 --> 00:19:06,552
(Gray: 7,313 dollars, 22 votes)

399
00:19:06,553 --> 00:19:07,653
(5,000 dollars deducted)

400
00:19:08,255 --> 00:19:11,224
(1 base vote, 5 extra votes)

401
00:19:11,926 --> 00:19:15,729
(Gray)

402
00:19:15,730 --> 00:19:18,165
(Gray: 7,313 dollars, 22 votes)

403
00:19:18,166 --> 00:19:20,534
(Gray: 7,313 dollars, 25 votes)

404
00:19:20,968 --> 00:19:22,435
Let me help Michael.

405
00:19:24,271 --> 00:19:26,939
(Gray gives three votes to Michael.)

406
00:19:26,940 --> 00:19:29,442
Please tell him about this later.

407
00:19:29,443 --> 00:19:33,046
The spy cannot convert
their accumulated personal funds...

408
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:34,747
into real prize money.

409
00:19:35,249 --> 00:19:39,018
The spy can only claim the prize pool...

410
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,821
if the residents fail the final challenge.

411
00:19:42,523 --> 00:19:43,823
I invested 3,000 dollars.

412
00:19:44,391 --> 00:19:45,759
I have no regrets...

413
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,593
because I will make
even more money tomorrow...

414
00:19:47,594 --> 00:19:50,063
by blowing that 3,000 dollars.

415
00:19:50,064 --> 00:19:51,831
It's an investment,

416
00:19:51,832 --> 00:19:53,399
so I don't feel bad about spending it now.

417
00:19:53,768 --> 00:19:56,536
I won't buy extra ballots.

418
00:19:59,607 --> 00:20:02,742
(The Final Favorability Vote)

419
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:05,612
This is an announcement
from the Community Center.

420
00:20:06,991 --> 00:20:10,492
We will now reveal
the current bottom three.

421
00:20:10,517 --> 00:20:11,885
They're just doing it like that?

422
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:13,853
Don't do that.

423
00:20:16,891 --> 00:20:18,491
The bottom three are...

424
00:20:18,492 --> 00:20:20,694
Sugar,

425
00:20:20,695 --> 00:20:23,196
Genie,

426
00:20:23,197 --> 00:20:25,999
and Ted.

427
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,434
- Then...
- That means...

428
00:20:27,435 --> 00:20:29,703
- It's not Michael.
- He's not one of them.

429
00:20:29,704 --> 00:20:30,770
He moved up a lot.

430
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:32,272
(The bottom three: Sugar, Genie, Ted)

431
00:20:32,273 --> 00:20:33,373
Do you have 24?

432
00:20:33,507 --> 00:20:34,607
(Current favorability score: 24)

433
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:36,709
That means Michael has a lot.

434
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:37,477
(Current favorability score: 22)

435
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:40,213
(Current favorability score: 21)

436
00:20:40,481 --> 00:20:43,783
(They don't know
how many votes each person has.)

437
00:20:45,053 --> 00:20:47,287
Michael, you're not in the bottom three.

438
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:50,223
- How many do you have now?
- I have 21 or 23.

439
00:20:50,224 --> 00:20:53,093
The bottom three were announced just now,
and they are Sugar, Genie, and Ted.

440
00:20:53,094 --> 00:20:55,495
Which means you have more than 21.

441
00:20:55,496 --> 00:20:56,830
I do.

442
00:20:56,831 --> 00:20:59,132
- I didn't lie.
- What if you have more than me?

443
00:20:59,133 --> 00:21:01,401
- No!
- I bought him three.

444
00:21:02,369 --> 00:21:04,537
- I bought him three votes.
- You have a lot too.

445
00:21:05,473 --> 00:21:06,573
I bought you three.

446
00:21:06,707 --> 00:21:07,607
Then...

447
00:21:08,242 --> 00:21:09,475
He got a lot of votes.

448
00:21:10,111 --> 00:21:12,345
- You bought me a lot.
- You have more than me.

449
00:21:13,247 --> 00:21:15,381
He's way behind in votes.

450
00:21:15,382 --> 00:21:16,382
I have 16.

451
00:21:17,418 --> 00:21:19,986
(His real favorability score: 18)

452
00:21:20,287 --> 00:21:21,754
Everyone has so many hearts.

453
00:21:22,556 --> 00:21:24,190
I didn't expect to be at the bottom.

454
00:21:25,092 --> 00:21:26,059
At the bottom?

455
00:21:26,627 --> 00:21:28,027
You lied to me.

456
00:21:28,262 --> 00:21:29,095
- Me?
- Yes.

457
00:21:29,096 --> 00:21:31,397
I told you I'm in the low 20s.

458
00:21:31,932 --> 00:21:34,067
- I didn't lie.
- But there was an announcement.

459
00:21:34,068 --> 00:21:35,568
Sugar has 24.

460
00:21:35,736 --> 00:21:36,736
No!

461
00:21:36,971 --> 00:21:40,840
I have 24. I know how many I have.

462
00:21:41,208 --> 00:21:43,176
- Really?
- You have more than that for sure.

463
00:21:43,344 --> 00:21:44,411
How many do you have?

464
00:21:44,879 --> 00:21:46,913
I poured in all my money,
but I'm still in the low 20s.

465
00:21:46,914 --> 00:21:49,149
That's all I'm going to say.

466
00:21:49,216 --> 00:21:52,218
Look. Go Ae Shin lied too, then.

467
00:21:52,219 --> 00:21:54,053
She told me she had 21.

468
00:21:54,054 --> 00:21:55,922
- After she bought some votes?
- She hasn't voted yet.

469
00:21:57,458 --> 00:21:58,391
I have 21.

470
00:21:58,392 --> 00:22:00,827
(Her real favorability score: 24)

471
00:22:01,729 --> 00:22:02,896
She's saving money.

472
00:22:02,897 --> 00:22:05,331
Everyone is lying. This is annoying.

473
00:22:08,402 --> 00:22:09,736
Should I buy 4 and make it 30?

474
00:22:09,737 --> 00:22:11,237
You have 26?

475
00:22:11,238 --> 00:22:13,406
(His current favorability score: 28)

476
00:22:14,308 --> 00:22:16,309
Why can't I trust anyone?

477
00:22:21,348 --> 00:22:22,916
As you probably know,

478
00:22:22,917 --> 00:22:25,017
I'm the type of person
who doesn't hide anything from people.

479
00:22:25,018 --> 00:22:27,853
But when I told them about my score,

480
00:22:27,854 --> 00:22:31,457
people knew that my score would become
a reference point for everyone.

481
00:22:31,458 --> 00:22:33,392
They probably knew...

482
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:34,727
I hadn't gotten...

483
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:36,862
that many hearts or saved up...

484
00:22:36,863 --> 00:22:37,797
that much money either.

485
00:22:37,798 --> 00:22:40,499
Whatever number I gave would've become
the benchmark,

486
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:44,136
so I gave them a lower number.

487
00:22:44,137 --> 00:22:45,538
Then when it all came down to it,

488
00:22:45,840 --> 00:22:49,141
the people at the bottom
started calling me a liar.

489
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:50,644
They might think,

490
00:22:50,645 --> 00:22:52,646
"He lied to save himself."

491
00:22:52,647 --> 00:22:54,113
"He was desperate to survive."

492
00:22:54,114 --> 00:22:55,682
But did anyone tell...

493
00:22:55,683 --> 00:22:57,317
the truth?

494
00:22:57,318 --> 00:22:59,687
I got all the blame...

495
00:22:59,688 --> 00:23:01,554
just because I wasn't 100 percent honest.

496
00:23:01,722 --> 00:23:03,322
That gave me chills.

497
00:23:03,323 --> 00:23:05,224
How two-faced they are.

498
00:23:05,926 --> 00:23:08,762
First of all, I only have 1,620 dollars.

499
00:23:08,763 --> 00:23:10,663
I can't afford extra ballots.

500
00:23:10,664 --> 00:23:13,534
I only have 18 votes.

501
00:23:13,535 --> 00:23:15,335
I'm most likely to get eliminated.

502
00:23:15,336 --> 00:23:18,137
So I used a little trick.

503
00:23:18,138 --> 00:23:21,173
When people asked me
what my score was, I said it was 16.

504
00:23:21,174 --> 00:23:23,209
I took two votes off...

505
00:23:23,210 --> 00:23:25,978
to make people feel a little bad for me.

506
00:23:25,979 --> 00:23:27,546
If you're completely honest,

507
00:23:27,547 --> 00:23:29,382
you end up putting yourself
at a disadvantage.

508
00:23:29,383 --> 00:23:30,850
That's the uncomfortable truth.

509
00:23:30,851 --> 00:23:33,019
How do I put this?
It was my little scheme.

510
00:23:33,421 --> 00:23:34,454
Please don't hate me.

511
00:23:35,489 --> 00:23:36,856
(Current Favorability Ranking)

512
00:23:36,857 --> 00:23:38,057
(Current eviction candidates)

513
00:23:38,058 --> 00:23:44,030
(The bottom three)

514
00:23:44,398 --> 00:23:46,866
(Michael)

515
00:23:48,469 --> 00:23:49,836
I have 27?

516
00:23:52,339 --> 00:23:55,041
(Ted)

517
00:23:55,376 --> 00:23:57,210
(Ted: 7,112 dollars, 20 votes)

518
00:23:57,211 --> 00:23:58,645
(One vote added)

519
00:23:59,146 --> 00:24:01,247
I'll buy two extra ballots.

520
00:24:01,715 --> 00:24:02,648
(Please stand by.)

521
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:04,417
(2,000 dollars deducted)

522
00:24:05,486 --> 00:24:07,120
(Michael)

523
00:24:07,121 --> 00:24:08,755
As for Michael,

524
00:24:09,190 --> 00:24:11,891
people made fun of him a lot,

525
00:24:11,892 --> 00:24:14,594
but he played a huge role
in exposing Benjamin...

526
00:24:14,762 --> 00:24:16,896
and lost everything he had in the process.

527
00:24:17,698 --> 00:24:19,899
I used my base vote on myself...

528
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:21,701
and spent 2,000 dollars...

529
00:24:21,702 --> 00:24:22,602
to get him two votes.

530
00:24:22,803 --> 00:24:24,737
Michael went through a lot,

531
00:24:24,738 --> 00:24:26,606
and we'd gotten pretty close.

532
00:24:26,607 --> 00:24:29,976
I voted for him because I wanted...

533
00:24:29,977 --> 00:24:30,977
to help him survive.

534
00:24:31,444 --> 00:24:33,279
I voted for Michael.

535
00:24:33,981 --> 00:24:37,283
(The residents answered his call
for help.)

536
00:24:37,851 --> 00:24:39,285
(Michael: 26 votes)

537
00:24:39,286 --> 00:24:41,020
(One vote added)

538
00:24:42,390 --> 00:24:43,256
That's so many.

539
00:24:44,425 --> 00:24:47,093
This community touched my heart today.

540
00:24:47,094 --> 00:24:50,363
I told them I was broke
and expressed how sad I was.

541
00:24:50,364 --> 00:24:52,732
They took it seriously
and thought about me.

542
00:24:52,966 --> 00:24:56,369
(The Final Favorability Vote)

543
00:24:56,370 --> 00:24:58,871
What if I invest all my money today
and we have a money battle tomorrow?

544
00:25:02,376 --> 00:25:03,209
Goodness.

545
00:25:03,811 --> 00:25:05,578
If I blow all my money
and become penniless,

546
00:25:05,579 --> 00:25:06,646
what's the point?

547
00:25:06,647 --> 00:25:07,447
I know.

548
00:25:07,448 --> 00:25:08,715
I don't even have that much.

549
00:25:09,283 --> 00:25:10,483
It was totally unexpected.

550
00:25:10,651 --> 00:25:12,552
I thought, "Sugar is in the bottom three?"

551
00:25:12,553 --> 00:25:14,687
"People must have already spent
quite a bit."

552
00:25:14,688 --> 00:25:16,689
She told me her score...

553
00:25:16,690 --> 00:25:18,491
after she voted.

554
00:25:18,492 --> 00:25:20,760
From what I'd seen over the past few days,

555
00:25:20,761 --> 00:25:23,563
the score should be pretty safe.

556
00:25:23,564 --> 00:25:25,032
If she's dropped all the way...

557
00:25:25,033 --> 00:25:27,000
to the bottom three in that short time,

558
00:25:27,001 --> 00:25:29,269
that means people spent a lot of money.

559
00:25:29,937 --> 00:25:32,238
How can the average be that high?

560
00:25:32,239 --> 00:25:33,640
I'm shocked.

561
00:25:33,641 --> 00:25:35,608
I also got burned by sitting back.

562
00:25:35,843 --> 00:25:38,411
Why is everyone lying?

563
00:25:38,745 --> 00:25:40,246
I knew it.

564
00:25:40,247 --> 00:25:42,215
I try to be honest...

565
00:25:42,216 --> 00:25:44,350
and always end up getting screwed over.

566
00:25:46,520 --> 00:25:50,389
I didn't expect Genie, Ted, and Sugar
to be in the bottom three.

567
00:25:50,390 --> 00:25:52,425
That works in my favor...

568
00:25:52,426 --> 00:25:54,293
because that gave them reason...

569
00:25:54,294 --> 00:25:56,729
to question each other.

570
00:25:56,864 --> 00:25:59,132
That makes it easier for me
to make a move.

571
00:25:59,433 --> 00:26:00,666
Are you going to buy more votes?

572
00:26:00,868 --> 00:26:03,236
I don't have much money left now.

573
00:26:03,670 --> 00:26:05,871
- How many did you get for Michael?
- I bought him three.

574
00:26:06,040 --> 00:26:07,207
Why did you buy so many?

575
00:26:07,208 --> 00:26:10,443
I had no choice.
We've been through a lot together.

576
00:26:10,577 --> 00:26:12,711
Sugar, Genie, and Ted are at the bottom.

577
00:26:12,712 --> 00:26:13,846
But...

578
00:26:13,847 --> 00:26:15,247
all of them lied.

579
00:26:15,248 --> 00:26:17,383
Even Go Ae Shin said she had 21.

580
00:26:18,052 --> 00:26:20,120
Everyone lied, so you can't trust anyone.

581
00:26:21,455 --> 00:26:22,354
Should I buy one more?

582
00:26:24,158 --> 00:26:25,358
To be honest, I'm not sure.

583
00:26:25,359 --> 00:26:27,961
Since everyone lied,
you can't really trust them.

584
00:26:29,997 --> 00:26:31,230
I don't know what you should do.

585
00:26:33,700 --> 00:26:36,268
To plant seeds of doubt,

586
00:26:36,737 --> 00:26:39,772
I pulled them aside one by one...

587
00:26:40,307 --> 00:26:42,475
and made them distrust each other.

588
00:26:42,476 --> 00:26:44,343
As you can see,

589
00:26:44,344 --> 00:26:46,279
I'm good at stirring up distrust.

590
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:47,380
Influencing people...

591
00:26:47,948 --> 00:26:48,814
and manipulating the group.

592
00:26:49,116 --> 00:26:52,852
Seems like some people are tied at 24,

593
00:26:54,121 --> 00:26:55,888
and you have more money than them.

594
00:26:56,490 --> 00:26:57,491
(Go Ae Shin won prize money...)

595
00:26:57,492 --> 00:26:58,991
You received 5,000 dollars earlier.

596
00:26:58,992 --> 00:27:00,092
(from the daytime mission.)

597
00:27:00,093 --> 00:27:02,628
If your scores are tied,
it comes down to money.

598
00:27:04,818 --> 00:27:07,733
(The residents who won 5,000 dollars
from the Life Speech mission)

599
00:27:08,335 --> 00:27:09,802
The people who didn't win 5,000 dollars...

600
00:27:09,971 --> 00:27:11,571
will be battling it out.

601
00:27:12,806 --> 00:27:13,939
Except those with a lot of money.

602
00:27:17,377 --> 00:27:18,611
What should I do?

603
00:27:18,612 --> 00:27:21,513
I should buy some ballots
because survival comes first, right?

604
00:27:22,549 --> 00:27:24,251
- I think you should buy two.
- Should I?

605
00:27:24,252 --> 00:27:25,184
I think you should.

606
00:27:25,953 --> 00:27:28,021
You should also buy two to be safe.

607
00:27:28,255 --> 00:27:29,655
Everyone is on their own here.

608
00:27:30,190 --> 00:27:33,058
If you have money,
you can buy your way out.

609
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:35,394
Isn't this literally the wealth gap?

610
00:27:36,031 --> 00:27:38,832
This is Gray. I'll buy two.

611
00:27:38,833 --> 00:27:40,500
(Gray: 5,313 dollars, 27 votes)

612
00:27:40,900 --> 00:27:42,434
One more ballot, please.

613
00:27:42,435 --> 00:27:43,936
(Superman: 12,302 dollars, 29 votes)

614
00:27:44,238 --> 00:27:46,239
(Giving Michael one vote as he promised)

615
00:27:46,240 --> 00:27:48,541
I'll buy extra ballots.

616
00:27:48,542 --> 00:27:49,909
I'll take three.

617
00:27:51,245 --> 00:27:53,413
(Go Ae Shin: 8,869 dollars, 24 votes)

618
00:27:53,414 --> 00:27:54,981
(Three votes added)

619
00:27:54,982 --> 00:28:01,955
(Current Favorability Ranking)

620
00:28:02,523 --> 00:28:04,958
- I should buy some too, right?
- Go for it.

621
00:28:05,926 --> 00:28:06,826
Two?

622
00:28:06,827 --> 00:28:08,527
That'd be the safer move.

623
00:28:10,164 --> 00:28:12,598
One more might not be enough.

624
00:28:12,733 --> 00:28:15,168
Genie, you have immunity,
so you must be torn too.

625
00:28:15,769 --> 00:28:17,035
That's why I'm conflicted.

626
00:28:17,638 --> 00:28:20,173
I have two options now.

627
00:28:20,874 --> 00:28:23,309
If I'm at the bottom,

628
00:28:23,577 --> 00:28:26,779
I could just surrender my immunity now
to keep the money and survive.

629
00:28:26,780 --> 00:28:30,049
I could be eliminated tomorrow morning.

630
00:28:30,317 --> 00:28:32,818
Then, there's no point
in holding onto my money now.

631
00:28:33,654 --> 00:28:35,421
If I blow all my money...

632
00:28:37,024 --> 00:28:38,758
and survive, great.

633
00:28:38,759 --> 00:28:41,160
But if I'm still at the bottom,

634
00:28:41,628 --> 00:28:43,862
I'd lose both my money and my immunity.

635
00:28:43,863 --> 00:28:46,498
Her safest move is
to sit back and do nothing.

636
00:28:46,499 --> 00:28:48,367
She doesn't have to do anything.

637
00:28:48,535 --> 00:28:52,404
I think I could survive if I bet, but...

638
00:28:52,405 --> 00:28:53,606
But you don't have much money.

639
00:28:53,607 --> 00:28:55,074
I don't have a lot of money.

640
00:28:55,577 --> 00:28:57,877
I knew Genie couldn't be eliminated.

641
00:28:58,111 --> 00:29:00,245
I had 21 votes,
so if I'd spent 5,000 dollars,

642
00:29:00,246 --> 00:29:02,081
I could've gotten it up to 26.

643
00:29:02,382 --> 00:29:04,183
I knew there were a few people...

644
00:29:04,418 --> 00:29:06,519
who'd definitely be eliminated
if I moved up.

645
00:29:06,787 --> 00:29:08,987
"If I made that move knowing all that,"

646
00:29:08,988 --> 00:29:12,259
"would I really be staying true
to what I believe?"

647
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:15,294
They told me the truth
because they trusted me.

648
00:29:15,862 --> 00:29:17,897
If I hadn't known,

649
00:29:17,898 --> 00:29:19,298
I would've just thrown my money in.

650
00:29:19,299 --> 00:29:22,568
Knowing what I knew,
it wouldn't be a fair fight.

651
00:29:22,803 --> 00:29:23,703
I'd just be slaughtering them.

652
00:29:23,704 --> 00:29:24,937
I kept going back and forth about it.

653
00:29:25,138 --> 00:29:26,572
I wonder what Sugar will do.

654
00:29:26,573 --> 00:29:28,907
I told Sugar to buy some more. She has to.

655
00:29:28,908 --> 00:29:30,976
I don't think Genie would buy more.

656
00:29:31,512 --> 00:29:32,745
- Because of her immunity?
- Yes.

657
00:29:32,746 --> 00:29:34,213
She's trying to keep the money.

658
00:29:34,882 --> 00:29:37,116
Genie is really something.

659
00:29:37,650 --> 00:29:39,385
She has immunity,

660
00:29:39,386 --> 00:29:41,487
and she's the most ambitious.

661
00:29:42,121 --> 00:29:43,956
I recommend you buy two more.

662
00:29:45,158 --> 00:29:47,259
Then only one person will be kicked out.

663
00:29:48,128 --> 00:29:49,495
Who would it be?

664
00:29:50,797 --> 00:29:52,965
(Sugar, current favorability score: 24,
the maximum attainable: 29)

665
00:29:52,966 --> 00:29:55,868
(Ted, current favorability score: 21,
the maximum attainable: 26)

666
00:29:56,136 --> 00:30:00,773
(The Final Favorability Vote)

667
00:30:08,215 --> 00:30:09,315
We have to make a decision.

668
00:30:09,316 --> 00:30:11,184
- We have to decide now.
- I know. We do.

669
00:30:27,934 --> 00:30:29,434
I closed my eyes...

670
00:30:29,435 --> 00:30:30,936
and gave it a lot of thought.

671
00:30:31,138 --> 00:30:32,572
We caught the spy.

672
00:30:32,573 --> 00:30:35,641
I've already gotten to experience a lot
of what I came here hoping for.

673
00:30:35,642 --> 00:30:37,877
A lot more people had made it this far.

674
00:30:37,951 --> 00:30:40,386
More than we'd expected at the beginning.

675
00:30:40,615 --> 00:30:43,249
From here on out, it's all about winning.

676
00:30:43,250 --> 00:30:44,884
That could be exciting,

677
00:30:45,152 --> 00:30:47,253
but is it really worth...

678
00:30:47,254 --> 00:30:49,721
joining this brutal battle...

679
00:30:49,722 --> 00:30:51,824
just to make it to tomorrow?

680
00:30:51,825 --> 00:30:53,793
If all that's left now is a fight
to the finish,

681
00:30:53,894 --> 00:30:55,761
maybe I don't mind being eliminated.

682
00:30:55,762 --> 00:30:57,196
They can fight it out among themselves.

683
00:30:58,265 --> 00:30:59,732
(The Final Favorability Vote)

684
00:31:03,236 --> 00:31:04,670
(The Final Favorability Vote)

685
00:31:07,674 --> 00:31:09,508
Then my hypocritical self came out.

686
00:31:18,585 --> 00:31:21,787
I kept debating it, but I ended up going
back to buy more votes.

687
00:31:22,221 --> 00:31:25,658
As I said, I'm a very curious person.

688
00:31:26,001 --> 00:31:28,260
We only had one day left.

689
00:31:28,261 --> 00:31:29,829
What's left at the end?

690
00:31:29,830 --> 00:31:33,332
Would it be a nightmare or something
more exciting than I expected?

691
00:31:33,333 --> 00:31:35,868
How many people would still be left?
I had so many questions.

692
00:31:36,203 --> 00:31:38,403
I started justifying myself.

693
00:31:38,404 --> 00:31:39,671
Whatever.

694
00:31:40,006 --> 00:31:42,774
I decided to make it a game
and see how things would play out...

695
00:31:42,775 --> 00:31:44,042
between Sugar and me.

696
00:31:44,043 --> 00:31:45,744
Let's see who makes it to the end.

697
00:31:46,213 --> 00:31:48,147
- We might not have enough time.
- I know.

698
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:52,785
Two minutes left...

699
00:31:53,153 --> 00:31:54,453
until voting closes.

700
00:31:54,454 --> 00:31:56,622
(The Final Favorability Vote)

701
00:31:59,192 --> 00:32:01,660
- This is so brutal.
- A game of wits.

702
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:06,265
(The Final Favorability Vote)

703
00:32:07,234 --> 00:32:09,936
- We should just accept it.
- Right.

704
00:32:10,804 --> 00:32:11,737
It's out of our hands.

705
00:32:13,240 --> 00:32:15,241
(The Final Favorability Vote)

706
00:32:18,111 --> 00:32:19,678
(Your vote is valid as long as you enter
before the time limit.)

707
00:32:19,679 --> 00:32:21,513
- Can I go first?
- Go ahead.

708
00:32:21,514 --> 00:32:22,648
Okay.

709
00:32:22,816 --> 00:32:24,383
- Did you buy some?
- Yes.

710
00:32:24,851 --> 00:32:26,953
If Sugar comes out,
and there's still time,

711
00:32:26,954 --> 00:32:28,086
I'll go for the win.

712
00:32:28,087 --> 00:32:30,055
(The Final Favorability Vote)

713
00:32:30,357 --> 00:32:33,559
I'll buy extra ballots.

714
00:32:34,027 --> 00:32:36,395
(The Final Favorability Vote)

715
00:32:36,563 --> 00:32:38,731
If I can enter after she comes out,

716
00:32:38,732 --> 00:32:39,665
it'll be a real showdown.

717
00:32:45,439 --> 00:32:46,305
Aren't you going in?

718
00:32:46,306 --> 00:32:47,940
I can't unless she comes out.

719
00:32:49,910 --> 00:32:52,411
(The Final Favorability Vote)

720
00:32:52,612 --> 00:32:53,545
It's closing soon.

721
00:33:00,487 --> 00:33:03,122
(The Final Favorability Vote)

722
00:33:03,590 --> 00:33:05,324
(Sugar: 1,196 dollars, 24 votes)

723
00:33:05,725 --> 00:33:07,225
(Sugar: 1,196 dollars, 28 votes)

724
00:33:07,693 --> 00:33:10,662
The final favorability vote is now closed.

725
00:33:10,663 --> 00:33:11,863
(The Final Favorability Vote: closed)

726
00:33:13,067 --> 00:33:15,534
- You have one second left!
- It's over. Let's go.

727
00:33:16,102 --> 00:33:17,436
- You didn't go, then?
- No.

728
00:33:17,437 --> 00:33:18,537
Neither of us could go in.

729
00:33:19,940 --> 00:33:21,473
Sugar is in there.

730
00:33:25,345 --> 00:33:27,279
The final eviction candidates are...

731
00:33:27,782 --> 00:33:33,318
Genie and Ted.

732
00:33:35,255 --> 00:33:36,755
Ted, I told you to go.

733
00:33:36,990 --> 00:33:38,857
I tried, but it's fine.

734
00:33:39,026 --> 00:33:42,294
Any resident who wishes
to transfer their immunity,

735
00:33:42,295 --> 00:33:44,496
please visit the Community Center...

736
00:33:44,497 --> 00:33:47,032
before it closes.

737
00:33:48,602 --> 00:33:50,336
It's a gamble.

738
00:33:52,305 --> 00:33:53,872
I kept my money.

739
00:33:59,813 --> 00:34:00,780
This is fun.

740
00:34:01,781 --> 00:34:02,914
No. I can't let you go.

741
00:34:02,915 --> 00:34:04,649
It's okay.

742
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:07,820
Ted.

743
00:34:07,855 --> 00:34:09,488
- Don't give up.
- It was my choice.

744
00:34:16,830 --> 00:34:17,897
This has been fun.

745
00:34:21,935 --> 00:34:25,705
Ted let me go in first.

746
00:34:25,706 --> 00:34:29,341
I feel bad that he sacrificed himself
for me.

747
00:34:29,643 --> 00:34:30,643
Good work.

748
00:34:35,582 --> 00:34:38,050
- Great work.
- Everyone went through a lot.

749
00:34:38,051 --> 00:34:40,419
We made it this far thanks to Ted.

750
00:34:40,420 --> 00:34:42,655
- I agree.
- He got us through a few tough times...

751
00:34:43,123 --> 00:34:45,324
with his quick thinking.

752
00:34:45,759 --> 00:34:48,026
I don't want to let him go.

753
00:34:48,027 --> 00:34:48,927
Me neither.

754
00:34:56,603 --> 00:34:58,170
I'll use my immunity card.

755
00:34:59,806 --> 00:35:01,173
(Please submit your immunity card.)

756
00:35:03,343 --> 00:35:06,512
(The last immunity card has been used.)

757
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:10,615
I wonder what the final game will be.

758
00:35:11,251 --> 00:35:12,384
I'm happy with how far I've come.

759
00:35:17,591 --> 00:35:19,024
I had a lot of fun.

760
00:35:19,292 --> 00:35:21,260
I had a great time.

761
00:35:21,261 --> 00:35:23,528
I do feel a sense of incompleteness...

762
00:35:23,763 --> 00:35:25,665
because I didn't make it
all the way to the end.

763
00:35:25,666 --> 00:35:28,500
I'm still curious about what the final day
would have been like.

764
00:35:28,501 --> 00:35:31,704
But I'm going home
with the sense of victory I wanted.

765
00:35:31,705 --> 00:35:33,372
We beat the spy.

766
00:35:33,373 --> 00:35:35,741
More people made it to the end...

767
00:35:35,742 --> 00:35:37,109
than we expected,

768
00:35:37,110 --> 00:35:38,210
and I feel like I contributed to that.

769
00:35:38,511 --> 00:35:41,680
I feel pretty accomplished
because of that.

770
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:44,183
I'm satisfied with how far I've made it.
Anything beyond this would be a bonus.

771
00:35:44,184 --> 00:35:47,252
I got to do almost everything...

772
00:35:47,253 --> 00:35:48,386
I wanted to do.

773
00:35:49,055 --> 00:35:51,657
If the only thing I missed was
finishing the game,

774
00:35:51,658 --> 00:35:53,892
I'd say I had a pretty good run.

775
00:35:54,094 --> 00:35:56,729
- Bye.
- Ted makes me emotional.

776
00:35:57,530 --> 00:35:58,897
- Goodbye.
- Stay in touch.

777
00:35:58,898 --> 00:36:00,198
Okay.

778
00:36:00,433 --> 00:36:01,333
Bye.

779
00:36:01,534 --> 00:36:02,534
Thanks, Ted.

780
00:36:02,535 --> 00:36:04,703
- Good luck, everyone.
- See you on the outside.

781
00:36:05,806 --> 00:36:07,672
Banu really got close to him.

782
00:36:07,907 --> 00:36:11,043
He really took care of her
more than anyone else,

783
00:36:11,044 --> 00:36:13,545
- Right.
- as if he were assigned to her.

784
00:36:17,617 --> 00:36:19,785
Before Ted got eliminated,

785
00:36:19,786 --> 00:36:24,089
I'd asked him how many hearts he had...

786
00:36:24,558 --> 00:36:27,259
because he helped me the most.

787
00:36:27,260 --> 00:36:28,728
(Banu: left, feminism,
upper-middle, conservative)

788
00:36:28,729 --> 00:36:30,029
He didn't tell me.

789
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:34,699
I wanted to buy him some votes,
but I couldn't even do that.

790
00:36:35,402 --> 00:36:37,136
He's really cool.

791
00:36:37,637 --> 00:36:39,771
Ted is not a hypocrite.

792
00:36:40,140 --> 00:36:43,309
He's a man of principle.

793
00:36:43,610 --> 00:36:45,778
Once he found out how many she had,

794
00:36:45,779 --> 00:36:48,014
I think he felt like...

795
00:36:48,015 --> 00:36:51,684
buying more than that would be unfair.

796
00:36:51,918 --> 00:36:53,853
This is good for me, though,

797
00:36:53,854 --> 00:36:57,256
because now we have one fewer person
who's really good at analyzing things.

798
00:36:57,457 --> 00:36:59,758
This makes things easier for the spy.

799
00:36:59,759 --> 00:37:02,127
That's a better way to look at it.

800
00:37:05,131 --> 00:37:06,965
(Evicted: Nangja, Benjamin, Ted, Hippo)

801
00:37:06,966 --> 00:37:10,302
(Ted: evicted)

802
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:12,704
How many do we have left?

803
00:37:12,705 --> 00:37:13,672
Nine.

804
00:37:14,207 --> 00:37:16,441
They could eliminate half of us at once.

805
00:37:16,776 --> 00:37:18,944
We aren't sure if they'll eliminate us...

806
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:21,847
or make us fight over each other's money.

807
00:37:24,317 --> 00:37:26,484
I think tomorrow will be about money.

808
00:37:27,687 --> 00:37:30,622
Maybe you made the right call
holding onto yours.

809
00:37:32,325 --> 00:37:36,111
I think tomorrow will involve the spy.

810
00:37:36,136 --> 00:37:37,729
The way I see it,

811
00:37:37,865 --> 00:37:41,700
the spy is definitely going
after someone tomorrow.

812
00:37:42,402 --> 00:37:44,136
I have a feeling...

813
00:37:45,071 --> 00:37:47,272
we'll be pitted against the spy.

814
00:38:02,822 --> 00:38:05,290
I've come this far. I'm seeing it through.

815
00:38:05,725 --> 00:38:07,759
I don't care what game we play tomorrow.

816
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:10,128
I'm going to win, no matter what.

817
00:38:22,976 --> 00:38:25,878
I was worried tomorrow might turn...

818
00:38:25,879 --> 00:38:27,546
into some kind of death match.

819
00:38:34,454 --> 00:38:35,788
Someone sharp...

820
00:38:36,389 --> 00:38:37,622
and articulate.

821
00:38:38,759 --> 00:38:39,691
And...

822
00:38:41,427 --> 00:38:42,427
And...

823
00:38:44,030 --> 00:38:45,130
And...

824
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:49,034
There isn't one.

825
00:38:51,638 --> 00:38:52,504
I'm...

826
00:38:54,707 --> 00:38:56,041
packing my bags,

827
00:38:57,711 --> 00:39:00,712
bracing for what's coming.

828
00:39:00,713 --> 00:39:01,981
I'm putting it all on the line...

829
00:39:02,115 --> 00:39:03,348
like my life depends on it.

830
00:39:04,951 --> 00:39:07,153
I could pit the rich against the poor,

831
00:39:07,154 --> 00:39:10,155
or match up people
who don't trust each other.

832
00:39:13,927 --> 00:39:16,061
Okay.

833
00:39:19,699 --> 00:39:21,767
Oh, boy.

834
00:39:33,346 --> 00:39:36,949
(The final morning)

835
00:39:41,154 --> 00:39:44,623
Today is the final day
at the Community House.

836
00:39:45,527 --> 00:39:48,827
The final game will begin shortly.

837
00:39:49,095 --> 00:39:51,930
Please stand by.

838
00:39:53,466 --> 00:39:55,400
I bet the final game is...

839
00:39:55,401 --> 00:39:58,503
about taking each other's money.

840
00:40:00,140 --> 00:40:02,141
I could play nice,

841
00:40:02,142 --> 00:40:03,942
or I could be ruthless.

842
00:40:03,943 --> 00:40:06,711
I have no idea what I'll do.

843
00:40:09,415 --> 00:40:11,816
I've made it this far.

844
00:40:12,619 --> 00:40:14,320
I'll do whatever it takes to survive.

845
00:40:21,895 --> 00:40:23,963
This won't be easy.

846
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:35,707
"Spy, please step forward to the center."

847
00:40:41,347 --> 00:40:44,749
Gray, the Community House spy.

848
00:40:45,686 --> 00:40:48,420
Welcome to the final game.

849
00:40:49,355 --> 00:40:53,658
The final game of the Community House
is "Dilemma Game."

850
00:40:55,061 --> 00:40:58,196
Residents can only take home
their prize money...

851
00:40:58,197 --> 00:41:01,033
if they win their two-player trust match.

852
00:41:02,603 --> 00:41:04,103
"Dilemma Game."

853
00:41:04,104 --> 00:41:10,909
The spy will decide
which two residents go head-to-head.

854
00:41:11,711 --> 00:41:14,680
Each resident will then decide...

855
00:41:14,681 --> 00:41:19,418
whether to share the money or take it all.

856
00:41:20,153 --> 00:41:23,788
If both players choose "Share,"

857
00:41:23,789 --> 00:41:26,092
their prize pots will be combined...

858
00:41:26,093 --> 00:41:28,127
and split right down the middle.

859
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:32,597
If one player chooses "Share"...

860
00:41:33,232 --> 00:41:35,901
and the other chooses "Keep,"

861
00:41:36,569 --> 00:41:41,106
the one who chose "Keep"
walks away with everything.

862
00:41:43,142 --> 00:41:46,678
If both choose "Keep,"

863
00:41:46,980 --> 00:41:50,916
the spy takes the entire pot.

864
00:41:52,251 --> 00:41:55,888
The spy stands to gain the most...

865
00:41:55,889 --> 00:42:00,558
by pairing up two residents
who don't trust each other.

866
00:42:02,996 --> 00:42:07,066
The Dilemma Game begins now.

867
00:42:07,700 --> 00:42:09,768
Spy, please submit...

868
00:42:09,769 --> 00:42:12,237
your player matchups.

869
00:42:14,340 --> 00:42:19,778
(The final daytime activity: Dilemma Game)

870
00:42:21,647 --> 00:42:25,151
Anyone sitting on a ton of cash
will definitely choose Keep.

871
00:42:28,021 --> 00:42:30,990
(Polar Bear's prize money: 5,556 dollars)

872
00:42:32,692 --> 00:42:35,694
(Superman's prize money: 12,302 dollars)

873
00:42:37,063 --> 00:42:40,132
(Dark Knight's prize money: 76 dollars)

874
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:44,202
(Michael's prize money: 620 dollars)

875
00:42:45,038 --> 00:42:48,374
(Sugar's prize money: 1,196 dollars)

876
00:42:51,577 --> 00:42:54,979
(Genie's prize money: 6,145 dollars)

877
00:42:55,915 --> 00:42:59,317
(Go Ae Shin's prize money: 8,869 dollars)

878
00:43:01,387 --> 00:43:04,723
(Banu's prize money: 9,594 dollars)

879
00:43:07,326 --> 00:43:09,261
I had two strategies.

880
00:43:09,262 --> 00:43:10,896
Based on what I'd observed,

881
00:43:10,897 --> 00:43:13,931
I sorted the trustworthy players
from the untrustworthy ones,

882
00:43:13,932 --> 00:43:16,167
and matched the rich players
with the broke ones.

883
00:43:16,168 --> 00:43:17,135
My logic was...

884
00:43:17,404 --> 00:43:20,772
the ones with a lot of money
would never risk choosing Share.

885
00:43:27,480 --> 00:43:31,183
(The two players are placed
in separate rooms.)

886
00:43:31,984 --> 00:43:34,686
(Match 1: Polar Bear vs. Superman)

887
00:43:34,854 --> 00:43:36,507
One person has 5,000 dollars,
another has 3,000 dollars,

888
00:43:36,531 --> 00:43:37,522
and the third has 1,000.

889
00:43:37,523 --> 00:43:39,257
Who do you eliminate?

890
00:43:39,258 --> 00:43:40,725
I'd rather not eliminate anyone.

891
00:43:41,060 --> 00:43:45,764
(Polar Bear and Superman have
never seen eye to eye.)

892
00:43:46,065 --> 00:43:47,366
What about you?

893
00:43:47,367 --> 00:43:50,769
Polar Bear is principled
and stands by her morals.

894
00:43:50,937 --> 00:43:55,074
If Superman had taken charge
and thrown his weight around,

895
00:43:55,075 --> 00:43:56,475
heads definitely would've rolled.

896
00:43:56,476 --> 00:44:02,047
I wanted to tap into their primal greed.

897
00:44:02,381 --> 00:44:04,248
Please remove your blindfolds.

898
00:44:10,923 --> 00:44:12,957
The matchup is set.

899
00:44:13,993 --> 00:44:16,261
The game begins now.

900
00:44:16,262 --> 00:44:17,896
(Match 1 begins.)

901
00:44:17,897 --> 00:44:21,299
(You're facing Superman.
Will you Share or Keep the money?)

902
00:44:25,104 --> 00:44:27,739
(You're facing Polar Bear.
Will you Share or Keep the money?)

903
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:30,608
The Prisoner's Dilemma.

904
00:44:31,310 --> 00:44:33,748
Put two suspects in separate rooms.

905
00:44:33,749 --> 00:44:35,580
Each tries to calculate
their prison sentence.

906
00:44:35,848 --> 00:44:37,615
The first one to turn gets immunity,

907
00:44:37,883 --> 00:44:39,951
and the other takes the fall.

908
00:44:40,319 --> 00:44:41,953
It was a textbook dilemma game.

909
00:44:42,555 --> 00:44:45,724
They literally gave us
the Prisoner's Dilemma.

910
00:44:46,292 --> 00:44:47,993
There's an obvious move here.

911
00:44:47,994 --> 00:44:49,828
Betrayal pays off in the short run.

912
00:44:49,829 --> 00:44:51,062
That's just math.

913
00:44:51,430 --> 00:44:54,632
One of the books on the shelf
was "Fermi Estimation."

914
00:44:54,767 --> 00:44:58,404
We haven't played anything
rooted in game theory yet.

915
00:44:58,405 --> 00:45:00,304
In game theory,

916
00:45:00,305 --> 00:45:03,074
the betrayer always wins
in the short term.

917
00:45:03,221 --> 00:45:04,109
On paper, at least.

918
00:45:04,378 --> 00:45:05,276
So...

919
00:45:06,612 --> 00:45:08,313
I drew Polar Bear.

920
00:45:08,681 --> 00:45:11,616
She is my exact opposite in every way.

921
00:45:12,051 --> 00:45:14,886
We both have the highest trust scores.

922
00:45:14,887 --> 00:45:16,588
I figured we got paired...

923
00:45:16,589 --> 00:45:18,056
because we're total opposites.

924
00:45:19,725 --> 00:45:21,661
It's way more fun
if they betray each other.

925
00:45:23,229 --> 00:45:24,162
Pull the trigger.

926
00:45:25,198 --> 00:45:28,700
(Share: roughly 8,930 dollars each)

927
00:45:28,701 --> 00:45:32,771
(Keep: roughly 17,860 dollars
for the winner)

928
00:45:34,874 --> 00:45:36,041
(Superman and Polar Bear are paired up.)

929
00:45:36,042 --> 00:45:36,975
(Their game begins now.)

930
00:45:37,343 --> 00:45:39,044
They're taking forever.

931
00:45:41,547 --> 00:45:43,448
(The results are ready.)

932
00:45:45,751 --> 00:45:47,351
Both players...

933
00:45:48,221 --> 00:45:50,055
chose Share.

934
00:45:50,189 --> 00:45:52,690
Exactly what I thought.

935
00:45:54,293 --> 00:45:55,759
Superman and Polar Bear.

936
00:45:55,760 --> 00:45:58,963
Knowing their backgrounds,

937
00:45:59,098 --> 00:46:02,067
I knew they wouldn't choose Keep,
no matter how much was at stake.

938
00:46:02,068 --> 00:46:04,769
So I just wrote that round off...

939
00:46:04,971 --> 00:46:06,438
to set up bigger gains later.

940
00:46:06,939 --> 00:46:09,574
(Polar Bear: 8,929 dollars won with Share)

941
00:46:09,909 --> 00:46:12,143
(Superman: 8,929 dollars won with Share)

942
00:46:12,311 --> 00:46:13,712
The premise of game theory is...

943
00:46:13,713 --> 00:46:16,815
that the traitor takes home
the biggest prize.

944
00:46:16,816 --> 00:46:19,251
If that's the setup,

945
00:46:19,252 --> 00:46:22,887
we have to remove the incentive to betray.

946
00:46:23,489 --> 00:46:25,857
The betrayer gets the biggest payout,

947
00:46:25,992 --> 00:46:27,726
but I couldn't bring myself to do it.

948
00:46:28,194 --> 00:46:32,241
I still catch myself thinking
about how much I could've pocketed...

949
00:46:32,266 --> 00:46:33,666
if I'd chosen Keep.

950
00:46:34,269 --> 00:46:36,402
But it wasn't my money to begin with.

951
00:46:36,636 --> 00:46:41,973
Superman had way more on the line
than I did.

952
00:46:41,974 --> 00:46:47,546
I'm sure it was
a much tougher call for him.

953
00:46:47,547 --> 00:46:49,414
I'm satisfied with the outcome.

954
00:46:50,416 --> 00:46:51,816
That matchup's done.

955
00:46:51,817 --> 00:46:52,951
(The spy gets zero money from Match 1.)

956
00:46:52,952 --> 00:46:56,020
Now I need two people with zero trust.

957
00:46:57,757 --> 00:46:59,892
Should I go for a double jackpot?

958
00:47:02,161 --> 00:47:03,761
They definitely don't trust each other.

959
00:47:04,196 --> 00:47:05,596
Go Ae Shin and Dark Knight.

960
00:47:12,578 --> 00:47:14,746
The one caught lying...

961
00:47:14,940 --> 00:47:16,274
was Dark Knight.

962
00:47:16,676 --> 00:47:19,278
Fine. I see why I look shady.

963
00:47:19,779 --> 00:47:23,682
(Dark Knight has failed to earn trust.)

964
00:47:24,350 --> 00:47:26,618
When it comes to loyalty, I don't flinch.

965
00:47:26,619 --> 00:47:30,088
If the person getting eliminated today
came and asked for it,

966
00:47:30,089 --> 00:47:32,056
I'd hand it right over.

967
00:47:32,057 --> 00:47:34,459
I can't just give away my immunity.

968
00:47:34,727 --> 00:47:36,695
Is there really anything
to hesitate about?

969
00:47:36,696 --> 00:47:38,096
Not at all.

970
00:47:38,097 --> 00:47:39,097
Then why call a meeting?

971
00:47:39,098 --> 00:47:41,933
(Go Ae Shin's actions
contradicted her words.)

972
00:47:42,068 --> 00:47:45,070
Go Ae Shin is ambitious,

973
00:47:45,071 --> 00:47:47,272
and she's sitting on a lot of money.

974
00:47:47,273 --> 00:47:49,507
There's no way she chooses Share.

975
00:47:49,508 --> 00:47:52,144
Especially after today,

976
00:47:52,169 --> 00:47:55,738
Dark Knight got caught
lying about his favorability score.

977
00:47:55,848 --> 00:47:59,584
And I threw fuel on the fire
once I caught him.

978
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:02,420
She doesn't trust him either,

979
00:48:02,755 --> 00:48:05,089
so if I throw them together,
they'll both hit Keep.

980
00:48:05,858 --> 00:48:10,395
In the final game, you will wager
your total accumulated prize money...

981
00:48:10,963 --> 00:48:13,631
and decide whether to split it evenly...

982
00:48:13,656 --> 00:48:17,693
or try to take it all for yourself.

983
00:48:19,004 --> 00:48:19,971
What is this?

984
00:48:20,272 --> 00:48:22,139
When the game ends,

985
00:48:22,474 --> 00:48:25,577
you will exit immediately...

986
00:48:25,578 --> 00:48:27,912
without seeing the other players.

987
00:48:29,815 --> 00:48:34,519
And with that, the Dilemma Game begins.

988
00:48:37,023 --> 00:48:39,023
The matchup is set.

989
00:48:39,258 --> 00:48:41,526
The game begins now.

990
00:48:42,862 --> 00:48:44,830
This is purely psychological.

991
00:48:47,266 --> 00:48:51,369
(Match 2: Go Ae Shin vs. Dark Knight)

992
00:48:52,638 --> 00:48:54,372
(You're facing Dark Knight.
Will you Share or Keep the money?)

993
00:48:54,373 --> 00:49:00,111
(Go Ae Shin: 8,870 dollars,
Dark Knight: 76 dollars)

994
00:49:03,849 --> 00:49:06,851
(A massive gap in prize money)

995
00:49:15,661 --> 00:49:16,728
Oh, man.

996
00:49:22,701 --> 00:49:24,902
(You're facing Go Ae Shin.
Will you Share or Keep the money?)

997
00:49:24,903 --> 00:49:27,171
(My pot: 76 dollars,
Go Ae Shin's pot: 8,869 dollars)

998
00:49:36,582 --> 00:49:39,951
(Go Ae Shin chooses Keep.)

999
00:49:40,619 --> 00:49:41,986
I can't look.

1000
00:49:43,155 --> 00:49:44,155
Are the results up?

1001
00:49:48,494 --> 00:49:50,295
(Waiting for the other player's decision)

1002
00:50:00,606 --> 00:50:02,273
I couldn't bring myself to look.

1003
00:50:02,408 --> 00:50:03,708
My mind was racing.

1004
00:50:03,709 --> 00:50:06,311
Dark Knight only had 80 bucks...

1005
00:50:06,312 --> 00:50:08,813
while I had 8,800.

1006
00:50:08,838 --> 00:50:11,306
If he had at least 3,000,
I would've chosen Share.

1007
00:50:11,383 --> 00:50:12,383
But 80?

1008
00:50:18,224 --> 00:50:19,090
(The results are ready.)

1009
00:50:19,091 --> 00:50:20,158
Here it comes.

1010
00:50:22,027 --> 00:50:23,929
I know for a fact they both picked Keep.

1011
00:50:29,769 --> 00:50:31,269
(Me: Keep, Opponent: Share)

1012
00:50:31,270 --> 00:50:35,640
(Dark Knight chose Share.)

1013
00:50:36,509 --> 00:50:39,945
(Go Ae Shin: 8,945 dollars won with Keep)

1014
00:50:40,613 --> 00:50:42,980
Dark Knight chose Share,

1015
00:50:42,981 --> 00:50:46,485
and Go Ae Shin chose Keep.

1016
00:50:46,486 --> 00:50:47,585
Dark Knight, man!

1017
00:50:48,187 --> 00:50:50,688
He completely blindsided me.

1018
00:50:52,591 --> 00:50:55,192
(The spy gets zero money from Match 2.)

1019
00:50:55,561 --> 00:50:57,696
Why would he do that?
He had nothing to lose.

1020
00:50:57,697 --> 00:50:59,764
He only had 76 bucks.

1021
00:51:00,499 --> 00:51:02,834
(One minute earlier)

1022
00:51:02,835 --> 00:51:04,302
Oh, man.

1023
00:51:08,674 --> 00:51:12,010
Whatever. Go Ae Shin, take it all.

1024
00:51:12,811 --> 00:51:14,578
(Dilemma Game)

1025
00:51:15,381 --> 00:51:16,247
(Me: Share, Opponent: Keep)

1026
00:51:16,248 --> 00:51:19,617
(Dark Knight: walks away with zero)

1027
00:51:21,287 --> 00:51:22,320
Definitely Share.

1028
00:51:22,821 --> 00:51:25,055
If I picked Keep,
she would've lost everything.

1029
00:51:25,391 --> 00:51:28,459
Stripping someone of all their money
out of pure greed?

1030
00:51:28,627 --> 00:51:30,528
I couldn't live with myself.

1031
00:51:30,930 --> 00:51:35,033
I remembered
what Go Ae Shin told me last night.

1032
00:51:35,601 --> 00:51:37,335
I kept telling them you weren't the spy.

1033
00:51:37,336 --> 00:51:38,937
But people still suspect me, right?

1034
00:51:38,938 --> 00:51:40,338
How many? Everyone?

1035
00:51:40,339 --> 00:51:41,272
Not everyone.

1036
00:51:42,041 --> 00:51:44,709
When everyone else suspected me,

1037
00:51:44,734 --> 00:51:46,301
she stood up for me.

1038
00:51:46,512 --> 00:51:49,981
My rule in life is
that if someone puts their trust in me,

1039
00:51:49,982 --> 00:51:51,816
I won't turn on them,

1040
00:51:51,817 --> 00:51:54,552
even if they lie to me.

1041
00:51:55,388 --> 00:51:56,855
Go Ae Shin, I just saved your life.

1042
00:51:56,856 --> 00:51:58,890
I do not betray someone
who puts their faith in me.

1043
00:51:58,891 --> 00:52:01,526
That is a core value I live by.

1044
00:52:01,527 --> 00:52:03,995
Take care of yourself out there.

1045
00:52:06,465 --> 00:52:09,233
I have to admit, a selfish thought
did cross my mind.

1046
00:52:09,569 --> 00:52:11,536
I dropped 3,000 dollars...

1047
00:52:11,537 --> 00:52:13,571
on favorability votes last night.

1048
00:52:13,973 --> 00:52:15,207
If I had not done that,

1049
00:52:15,541 --> 00:52:17,484
I would be sitting on
over 10,000 dollars right now!

1050
00:52:17,509 --> 00:52:18,677
It might sound greedy,

1051
00:52:18,678 --> 00:52:21,246
but a million thoughts raced
through my head right then.

1052
00:52:22,548 --> 00:52:25,850
Why did Dark Knight
break character like that?

1053
00:52:26,185 --> 00:52:28,653
Did he actually expect half her money?

1054
00:52:30,222 --> 00:52:31,689
That is pathetic.

1055
00:52:33,692 --> 00:52:35,826
My wild card backfired.

1056
00:52:39,632 --> 00:52:41,066
Now things get tricky.

1057
00:52:41,600 --> 00:52:44,235
I need to manipulate them
into picking Keep.

1058
00:52:47,874 --> 00:52:49,774
Please remove your blindfolds.

1059
00:52:53,312 --> 00:52:55,613
In this final game, you will put...

1060
00:52:55,614 --> 00:52:57,949
your total accumulated prize money
on the line...

1061
00:52:57,950 --> 00:53:01,219
and choose between Share and Keep.

1062
00:53:02,855 --> 00:53:06,491
Both pots will be combined...

1063
00:53:06,492 --> 00:53:08,793
and split right down the middle.

1064
00:53:10,396 --> 00:53:11,763
And here we go.

1065
00:53:11,764 --> 00:53:13,965
If one player chooses "Share"...

1066
00:53:14,333 --> 00:53:16,067
Once the game concludes,

1067
00:53:16,468 --> 00:53:19,537
you will exit immediately...

1068
00:53:19,538 --> 00:53:21,806
without seeing the other players.

1069
00:53:23,476 --> 00:53:27,812
With that, the Dilemma Game begins.

1070
00:53:28,714 --> 00:53:29,781
No way!

1071
00:53:29,782 --> 00:53:30,782
(Match 3 begins.)

1072
00:53:30,783 --> 00:53:33,284
I was the one who brought this up.

1073
00:53:33,285 --> 00:53:36,121
I noticed a book called "Game Theory"...
and the Prisoner's Dilemma was in it.

1074
00:53:36,122 --> 00:53:38,389
I told everyone
we would end up playing it.

1075
00:53:38,891 --> 00:53:41,192
And here we are.

1076
00:53:41,927 --> 00:53:43,095
I can't help but laugh.

1077
00:53:44,530 --> 00:53:47,165
It really came down
to the Prisoner's Dilemma.

1078
00:53:47,700 --> 00:53:48,900
Unbelievable.

1079
00:53:51,303 --> 00:53:52,303
Wait, what?

1080
00:53:54,239 --> 00:53:55,841
(Genie: 6,140 dollars,
Michael: 620 dollars)

1081
00:53:55,842 --> 00:53:57,975
Look at that gap.

1082
00:54:02,047 --> 00:54:05,750
(Michael is paired with Genie.)

1083
00:54:09,254 --> 00:54:10,921
Now this is interesting.

1084
00:54:15,060 --> 00:54:17,328
The difference is insane!

1085
00:54:17,329 --> 00:54:19,363
I went out of my way to save money.

1086
00:54:20,532 --> 00:54:21,567
This is completely unfair.

1087
00:54:23,469 --> 00:54:26,904
I only have 620 dollars anyway.

1088
00:54:31,376 --> 00:54:32,943
What is he going to pick?

1089
00:54:34,513 --> 00:54:37,615
What will Genie pick?

1090
00:54:40,018 --> 00:54:41,352
Genie, please choose Share.

1091
00:54:43,423 --> 00:54:46,825
Are you kidding? He only has 620 dollars.

1092
00:54:49,628 --> 00:54:51,896
This is infuriating.

1093
00:54:55,167 --> 00:54:57,268
What is taking so long?

1094
00:54:58,504 --> 00:54:59,504
Genie.

1095
00:55:03,041 --> 00:55:05,075
If he chooses Share,

1096
00:55:05,745 --> 00:55:08,045
he walks away with 3,000 dollars.

1097
00:55:08,781 --> 00:55:10,248
If he hits Keep...

1098
00:55:11,984 --> 00:55:13,818
Our combined money?

1099
00:55:14,419 --> 00:55:15,285
My money?

1100
00:55:16,121 --> 00:55:17,155
This is ridiculous!

1101
00:55:18,657 --> 00:55:21,192
I bet he picks Keep.

1102
00:55:21,928 --> 00:55:24,662
With only 620 dollars,
he has nothing to lose.

1103
00:55:26,331 --> 00:55:28,066
Both of you, just pick Keep.

1104
00:55:29,268 --> 00:55:31,970
He will roll the dice and pick Keep.

1105
00:55:34,173 --> 00:55:35,073
No.

1106
00:55:37,376 --> 00:55:38,576
Keep is my only move.

1107
00:55:38,844 --> 00:55:43,247
(Michael chooses Keep.)

1108
00:55:43,515 --> 00:55:45,683
Either we both walk away empty-handed,
or I take everything.

1109
00:55:45,684 --> 00:55:47,551
All or nothing, Genie.

1110
00:55:48,520 --> 00:55:50,354
Genie, hit Share.

1111
00:55:52,391 --> 00:55:53,758
No matter what I do,

1112
00:55:55,227 --> 00:55:56,627
I am losing money.

1113
00:55:59,464 --> 00:56:00,664
Genie.

1114
00:56:00,665 --> 00:56:02,699
I know you are picking Keep.

1115
00:56:05,304 --> 00:56:06,972
Right. I am going to lose it regardless.

1116
00:56:07,773 --> 00:56:11,075
(Genie chooses Keep.)

1117
00:56:12,377 --> 00:56:17,081
Both residents chose Keep.

1118
00:56:17,082 --> 00:56:18,449
I called it.

1119
00:56:18,684 --> 00:56:21,852
- The spy takes the prize money.
- Yes!

1120
00:56:22,789 --> 00:56:26,991
Michael has been badmouthing Genie
for days now.

1121
00:56:26,992 --> 00:56:28,793
"She is way too greedy."

1122
00:56:28,794 --> 00:56:30,695
"Money is all she cares about."

1123
00:56:30,696 --> 00:56:33,297
"Gray, why don't we team up
and take Genie down tomorrow?"

1124
00:56:33,298 --> 00:56:34,398
Those were his exact words.

1125
00:56:34,399 --> 00:56:35,967
(Gray, the spy)

1126
00:56:35,968 --> 00:56:39,270
I knew if I paired them up,

1127
00:56:39,271 --> 00:56:41,339
Michael would burn it all down.

1128
00:56:41,841 --> 00:56:44,975
Genie is fiercely ambitious,

1129
00:56:44,976 --> 00:56:47,778
so she would never pick Share either.

1130
00:56:47,779 --> 00:56:49,647
I was 100 percent certain of this outcome.

1131
00:56:49,648 --> 00:56:51,815
Just as planned, the pot is mine.

1132
00:56:52,718 --> 00:56:55,987
- Both players chose Keep.
- Are you kidding me?

1133
00:56:56,321 --> 00:56:59,023
The spy takes the combined prize pool.

1134
00:56:59,024 --> 00:57:00,357
This is unbelievable.

1135
00:57:01,827 --> 00:57:04,061
The spy gets it all?

1136
00:57:05,097 --> 00:57:07,532
(Genie: loses everything by choosing Keep)

1137
00:57:07,933 --> 00:57:10,268
"The spy gets the money?"

1138
00:57:14,139 --> 00:57:17,007
(Michael: loses everything
by choosing Keep)

1139
00:57:18,511 --> 00:57:20,144
Her greed is limitless...

1140
00:57:20,345 --> 00:57:22,346
like a bottomless pit.

1141
00:57:22,681 --> 00:57:24,882
I'm pretty sure...

1142
00:57:24,883 --> 00:57:27,151
I was the only target
the spy eliminated...

1143
00:57:27,152 --> 00:57:30,187
just because I spoke out from day one.

1144
00:57:30,188 --> 00:57:33,824
And I did not get a dime for it.

1145
00:57:33,825 --> 00:57:36,093
Polar Bear saved me,

1146
00:57:36,094 --> 00:57:39,830
and Gray spent 3,000 dollars
to keep me alive yesterday.

1147
00:57:39,831 --> 00:57:41,866
Superman voted for me.

1148
00:57:41,867 --> 00:57:43,334
Sugar backed me up,

1149
00:57:43,335 --> 00:57:44,802
and so did Ted.

1150
00:57:44,986 --> 00:57:46,236
I only wanted one thing.

1151
00:57:46,237 --> 00:57:48,806
A little bit of respect.

1152
00:57:49,107 --> 00:57:51,742
She was the only person
who never showed an ounce of gratitude.

1153
00:57:51,877 --> 00:57:54,712
Now she is stuck with me,

1154
00:57:54,713 --> 00:57:56,581
and it is her worst nightmare.

1155
00:57:56,748 --> 00:57:58,783
"You aren't walking away with that cash."

1156
00:57:59,051 --> 00:58:02,853
No way am I letting her win that money
and feast on Peking duck.

1157
00:58:02,854 --> 00:58:04,923
Not on my watch.

1158
00:58:08,226 --> 00:58:10,093
This is infuriating.

1159
00:58:10,094 --> 00:58:12,196
- What is this?
- The Dilemma Game is over.

1160
00:58:13,966 --> 00:58:15,466
Who is the spy?

1161
00:58:15,467 --> 00:58:17,334
The Community House...

1162
00:58:17,536 --> 00:58:21,538
will cherish the memories made here
with all of you.

1163
00:58:23,075 --> 00:58:24,375
Farewell.

1164
00:58:24,376 --> 00:58:27,612
Are you serious? This is ridiculous!

1165
00:58:28,580 --> 00:58:31,082
I am so furious right now!

1166
00:58:31,605 --> 00:58:32,816
Unbelievable.

1167
00:58:35,020 --> 00:58:36,554
I'm...

1168
00:58:37,489 --> 00:58:38,789
so mad I can't even think straight.

1169
00:58:38,790 --> 00:58:42,960
(Genie: right, feminism,
upper-middle, conservative)

1170
00:58:43,361 --> 00:58:46,064
I'm so angry I could burst into tears.

1171
00:58:46,665 --> 00:58:48,600
I'm livid. Wait a second.

1172
00:58:55,841 --> 00:58:57,975
Michael only had 600 dollars.

1173
00:58:58,243 --> 00:59:01,179
How shameless can you be,
gunning for 6,000 dollars?

1174
00:59:02,280 --> 00:59:03,280
Unbelievable.

1175
00:59:03,349 --> 00:59:06,250
You should have given me a fair matchup!

1176
00:59:06,718 --> 00:59:09,853
The sheer nerve of him to choose Keep.

1177
00:59:10,688 --> 00:59:12,390
Why would I ever choose Share?

1178
00:59:13,192 --> 00:59:15,526
The audacity of him
thinking he could hit Keep!

1179
00:59:16,094 --> 00:59:19,096
Has he no shame? Is he out of his mind?

1180
00:59:19,498 --> 00:59:22,367
What risk does the spy even take?

1181
00:59:22,600 --> 00:59:25,702
All reward, zero risk.

1182
00:59:26,238 --> 00:59:27,505
I should have been the spy!

1183
00:59:28,206 --> 00:59:29,873
They must be walking away with a fortune.

1184
00:59:30,042 --> 00:59:32,543
Who did Benjamin pick?

1185
00:59:32,778 --> 00:59:34,912
If anyone deserves that money,

1186
00:59:35,814 --> 00:59:37,882
it should be Benjamin...

1187
00:59:37,883 --> 00:59:42,019
since he actually put in the work
as the spy.

1188
00:59:42,320 --> 00:59:44,755
I would rather lose it to him
than some substitute...

1189
00:59:44,856 --> 00:59:46,990
who did nothing until yesterday...

1190
00:59:46,991 --> 00:59:48,492
and just sweeps in to rob me blind.

1191
00:59:48,660 --> 00:59:50,894
The spy appointed yesterday...

1192
00:59:50,895 --> 00:59:52,363
is absolute trash.

1193
00:59:52,697 --> 00:59:53,930
The ultimate snake.

1194
00:59:54,032 --> 00:59:55,967
We are done after this.

1195
00:59:58,670 --> 01:00:03,841
(The spy claims 6,765 dollars.)

1196
01:00:06,244 --> 01:00:07,444
Lastly...

1197
01:00:09,648 --> 01:00:12,017
This chemistry is going to be explosive.

1198
01:00:12,053 --> 01:00:13,351
Banu and Sugar.

1199
01:00:16,288 --> 01:00:18,656
(Match 4: Banu vs. Sugar)

1200
01:00:19,758 --> 01:00:23,394
(Banu: 9,600 dollars,
Sugar: 1,200 dollars)

1201
01:00:23,962 --> 01:00:27,031
Banu has so much money
that if she hits Share...

1202
01:00:27,032 --> 01:00:30,100
and her opponent hits Keep,
she loses every single cent.

1203
01:00:37,275 --> 01:00:38,976
This is brutal.

1204
01:00:39,311 --> 01:00:42,613
The silence was suffocating.

1205
01:00:42,949 --> 01:00:43,881
This is...

1206
01:00:43,882 --> 01:00:47,785
I expected an intense,
face-to-face showdown.

1207
01:00:47,786 --> 01:00:49,887
Instead, I was trapped in total isolation,

1208
01:00:49,888 --> 01:00:53,157
locked in cutthroat competition...

1209
01:00:53,325 --> 01:00:57,061
with someone in the other room.
It felt cruel.

1210
01:00:57,429 --> 01:00:59,797
(You're facing Banu.
Will you Share or Keep the money?)

1211
01:01:06,204 --> 01:01:08,339
I tried looking at it
from her perspective.

1212
01:01:08,340 --> 01:01:10,574
If I were sitting
on 9,000 dollars right now,

1213
01:01:10,575 --> 01:01:14,611
and my opponent had 1,000 dollars,
what move would I make?

1214
01:01:15,647 --> 01:01:16,747
Sugar.

1215
01:01:22,254 --> 01:01:23,254
Seriously.

1216
01:01:29,427 --> 01:01:33,430
(Share)

1217
01:01:33,965 --> 01:01:34,865
I trust you.

1218
01:01:36,701 --> 01:01:37,701
This is madness.

1219
01:01:42,607 --> 01:01:44,274
Sugar!

1220
01:01:44,350 --> 01:01:45,750
Let your greed take over!

1221
01:01:46,578 --> 01:01:49,414
(The results are ready.)

1222
01:01:49,415 --> 01:01:51,782
Banu chose Share,

1223
01:01:52,117 --> 01:01:55,519
and Sugar chose Keep.

1224
01:01:56,122 --> 01:01:57,054
Banu!

1225
01:01:59,224 --> 01:02:00,724
Banu, no!

1226
01:02:00,725 --> 01:02:02,293
(The spy gets zero money from Match 4.)

1227
01:02:02,828 --> 01:02:05,163
Banu, why on earth would you choose Share
with 10,000 dollars on the line?

1228
01:02:07,999 --> 01:02:10,167
I'm a hypocrite.

1229
01:02:10,168 --> 01:02:11,935
(Sugar: right, equalism,
upper-middle, open-minded)

1230
01:02:12,204 --> 01:02:13,738
The biggest hypocrite alive.

1231
01:02:15,340 --> 01:02:16,807
My options were walking away with nothing,

1232
01:02:16,975 --> 01:02:18,876
picking Share and taking 5,000 dollars,

1233
01:02:19,545 --> 01:02:23,548
or smashing Keep, winning the round,
and pocketing 10,000 dollars.

1234
01:02:23,549 --> 01:02:26,116
I only had 1,000 dollars,
so my thought process was...

1235
01:02:26,117 --> 01:02:28,185
I either leave empty-handed,

1236
01:02:28,186 --> 01:02:31,656
or I go for the entire 10,000 dollars.

1237
01:02:31,657 --> 01:02:33,558
I took the gamble.

1238
01:02:33,758 --> 01:02:36,027
I'm a total hypocrite for choosing Keep.

1239
01:02:36,461 --> 01:02:38,529
(Me: Share, Opponent: Keep)

1240
01:02:38,530 --> 01:02:41,398
(Banu: walks away with zero)

1241
01:02:42,100 --> 01:02:47,805
I was over 90 percent sure
she would pick Keep.

1242
01:02:48,107 --> 01:02:52,209
Her behavior yesterday completely
changed my opinion of her.

1243
01:02:52,210 --> 01:02:54,979
Up until then,
she seemed genuinely invested...

1244
01:02:54,980 --> 01:02:57,248
in reaching the finale together.

1245
01:02:57,249 --> 01:03:01,018
But when she faced elimination
alongside Ted yesterday,

1246
01:03:01,019 --> 01:03:04,988
I saw her greed come out.

1247
01:03:04,989 --> 01:03:08,526
If I had chosen Keep too,
neither of us would get a thing.

1248
01:03:08,660 --> 01:03:10,561
So I chose Share instead.

1249
01:03:10,729 --> 01:03:12,929
I figured she could treat me
to dinner sometime.

1250
01:03:13,666 --> 01:03:15,700
That was why I went with Share.

1251
01:03:19,871 --> 01:03:21,439
Unbelievable, Sugar!

1252
01:03:23,141 --> 01:03:24,942
I'm so screwed.

1253
01:03:25,176 --> 01:03:27,477
My heart aches for Banu.

1254
01:03:29,281 --> 01:03:30,381
Banu, why?

1255
01:03:31,416 --> 01:03:32,716
Sugar only had 1,000 dollars.

1256
01:03:32,717 --> 01:03:34,586
Why would Banu ever choose Share?

1257
01:03:35,053 --> 01:03:38,055
I should have pitted
Go Ae Shin against Sugar.

1258
01:03:38,056 --> 01:03:40,891
(Personal Funds Status)

1259
01:03:41,760 --> 01:03:43,861
The Dilemma Game has concluded.

1260
01:03:44,429 --> 01:03:48,733
This marks the end of all scheduled events
at the Community House.

1261
01:03:50,069 --> 01:03:55,573
The remaining 14,350 dollars
in the community fund...

1262
01:03:55,741 --> 01:03:58,209
will be distributed equally
among all residents,

1263
01:03:58,677 --> 01:04:01,512
excluding the spy.

1264
01:04:01,513 --> 01:04:05,482
- We get to split it?
- The payout each resident will receive...

1265
01:04:05,483 --> 01:04:09,787
from the community fund is 1,793 dollars.

1266
01:04:10,422 --> 01:04:12,256
I should have poured every cent
into the community fund.

1267
01:04:12,257 --> 01:04:14,158
Outstanding work, everyone.

1268
01:04:14,860 --> 01:04:18,662
The Community House will forever
cherish the memories...

1269
01:04:19,030 --> 01:04:21,198
we created together.

1270
01:04:22,334 --> 01:04:23,668
Farewell.

1271
01:04:28,606 --> 01:04:30,474
(Top Prize Winner: Sugar, 12,583 dollars)

1272
01:04:30,475 --> 01:04:32,542
(Final prize includes
share of community fund.)

1273
01:04:36,014 --> 01:04:39,917
I walked away with 6,765 dollars.

1274
01:04:40,785 --> 01:04:42,053
It could have been higher.

1275
01:04:42,787 --> 01:04:45,356
Sugar took the grand prize.

1276
01:04:45,758 --> 01:04:47,258
It came out to 6,760 dollars.

1277
01:04:47,726 --> 01:04:50,027
After everything I endured, this is it?

1278
01:04:50,295 --> 01:04:52,229
Does the spy get a bonus?

1279
01:04:52,430 --> 01:04:55,032
I kept begging them
to spend the community fund.

1280
01:04:55,033 --> 01:04:56,534
We blew through it all, didn't we?

1281
01:04:56,568 --> 01:04:59,803
(They spent 3,700 dollars
on last night's wrap-up party.)

1282
01:05:00,439 --> 01:05:01,705
They get to split it?

1283
01:05:01,706 --> 01:05:02,673
Without me?

1284
01:05:02,674 --> 01:05:05,309
(Gray, the spy)

1285
01:05:05,443 --> 01:05:08,078
This is awful.

1286
01:05:08,213 --> 01:05:09,489
How much is it per person, then?

1287
01:05:09,514 --> 01:05:10,849
Around 1,500 dollars each.

1288
01:05:11,649 --> 01:05:13,783
Let them take it.

1289
01:05:30,368 --> 01:05:33,237
(The flawless utopia of our dreams
does not exist.)

1290
01:05:33,238 --> 01:05:36,206
These nine days felt like...

1291
01:05:36,207 --> 01:05:40,477
a condensed reflection of my own life.

1292
01:05:40,478 --> 01:05:44,615
Some people watched nearly 10,000 dollars
vanish in a second today.

1293
01:05:44,949 --> 01:05:46,816
As you saw, I only lost 70 dollars.

1294
01:05:48,252 --> 01:05:51,321
Who walked away
with more peace of mind, them or me?

1295
01:05:51,556 --> 01:05:53,857
Money only carries value
when there is weight behind it.

1296
01:05:53,858 --> 01:05:57,628
If you just toss money around,
giving and taking it without consequence,

1297
01:05:58,096 --> 01:06:01,565
it loses all meaning.

1298
01:06:01,966 --> 01:06:03,901
This was my first survival show,

1299
01:06:03,902 --> 01:06:05,769
and people told me
to treat everyone as a threat.

1300
01:06:05,770 --> 01:06:07,704
"Don't trust anyone."

1301
01:06:07,705 --> 01:06:09,005
"Secure three allies right away."

1302
01:06:09,006 --> 01:06:11,241
I wrote down my 10 core rules
before arriving.

1303
01:06:11,377 --> 01:06:12,910
Whenever I started to lose my compass,
I reread them.

1304
01:06:12,911 --> 01:06:15,279
"This is nothing. Let it go."

1305
01:06:15,280 --> 01:06:18,233
Honestly, seeing everyone's
ideological codes upfront...

1306
01:06:18,258 --> 01:06:20,217
naturally gave me certain expectations.

1307
01:06:20,218 --> 01:06:23,253
Some people fit the mold exactly,

1308
01:06:23,254 --> 01:06:26,457
while others shattered
every assumption I made.

1309
01:06:26,458 --> 01:06:28,225
It made me realize
everyone is simply human.

1310
01:06:28,226 --> 01:06:30,728
We are all just individuals
navigating our own worldviews.

1311
01:06:31,264 --> 01:06:33,364
There were deeply uncomfortable moments,

1312
01:06:33,365 --> 01:06:35,232
and Michael was often the catalyst...

1313
01:06:35,567 --> 01:06:37,368
bringing those underlying tensions
to the surface.

1314
01:06:38,937 --> 01:06:42,940
I learned that lasting harmony sometimes
requires dragging discomfort...

1315
01:06:42,941 --> 01:06:46,710
out into the daylight to be addressed.

1316
01:06:47,078 --> 01:06:51,214
It proved to me
that genuine friendship is possible...

1317
01:06:51,215 --> 01:06:56,787
even across deep divides
in values and beliefs.

1318
01:06:57,555 --> 01:07:01,758
The experience felt
like studying abroad again.

1319
01:07:01,759 --> 01:07:03,927
You're dropped into an unfamiliar culture,

1320
01:07:04,195 --> 01:07:05,829
everything operates by foreign rules,

1321
01:07:05,830 --> 01:07:07,574
and no matter what you do,
you remain an outsider.

1322
01:07:07,599 --> 01:07:10,968
Arriving on day one
would have changed everything.

1323
01:07:10,969 --> 01:07:14,905
I wish I had been an original resident
from the start.

1324
01:07:15,173 --> 01:07:19,042
This experience offered
an extraordinary education.

1325
01:07:19,043 --> 01:07:20,878
Concepts I understood only in theory,

1326
01:07:20,879 --> 01:07:23,413
like the structural logic
behind the Constitution...

1327
01:07:23,414 --> 01:07:26,650
or why governance demands
checks and balances,

1328
01:07:26,819 --> 01:07:28,853
used to seem like distant rules...

1329
01:07:29,153 --> 01:07:34,090
created for abstract historical reasons.

1330
01:07:34,625 --> 01:07:37,495
Now I understand their
functional necessity on a systemic level.

1331
01:07:37,962 --> 01:07:41,398
Every strategic choice made here,

1332
01:07:41,399 --> 01:07:43,600
along with every
interpersonal negotiation,

1333
01:07:43,635 --> 01:07:50,641
will serve as an invaluable foundation
for my future in politics.

1334
01:07:51,643 --> 01:07:56,146
Leadership requires taking heat
and making the calls nobody wants to make.

1335
01:07:56,414 --> 01:07:58,348
Life was far simpler
as an ordinary resident.

1336
01:07:58,449 --> 01:08:00,818
The most agonizing dilemma...

1337
01:08:00,819 --> 01:08:05,689
was determining whether to grant immunity
to Michael or Hippo.

1338
01:08:05,690 --> 01:08:07,358
Should I have dictated the outcome,

1339
01:08:07,359 --> 01:08:09,527
or left the decision to them?

1340
01:08:09,528 --> 01:08:11,795
The weight of that trade-off was immense.

1341
01:08:11,796 --> 01:08:13,731
Afterward, Michael treated me
with unmatched generosity.

1342
01:08:15,500 --> 01:08:17,701
The trust I gained from him
was substantial.

1343
01:08:18,002 --> 01:08:21,504
I never imagined building
such a close bond with him.

1344
01:08:21,505 --> 01:08:24,508
Now he insists on staying
in regular contact outside.

1345
01:08:24,809 --> 01:08:25,966
Reflecting on it,

1346
01:08:25,991 --> 01:08:29,714
I have spent most of my life
surrounded by peers...

1347
01:08:29,739 --> 01:08:32,249
who share my exact
ideological perspective.

1348
01:08:32,377 --> 01:08:34,820
Here, I encountered people
from entirely disparate realities...

1349
01:08:34,852 --> 01:08:36,586
with opposing systems of thought.

1350
01:08:36,587 --> 01:08:38,988
Building interpersonal bonds first,

1351
01:08:38,989 --> 01:08:42,792
before uncovering
their underlying doctrines,

1352
01:08:42,862 --> 01:08:46,196
allowed us to actually absorb
different worldviews.

1353
01:08:46,197 --> 01:08:48,699
Surprisingly,
the most persuasive arguments...

1354
01:08:48,700 --> 01:08:50,935
came from those
whose beliefs clashed with mine.

1355
01:08:50,936 --> 01:08:53,971
They forced me to re-examine blind spots
I had never questioned.

1356
01:08:54,405 --> 01:08:56,405
A preconception is
merely an unverified assumption.

1357
01:08:56,406 --> 01:08:59,075
Divergent perspectives are
simply alternative lenses.

1358
01:08:59,076 --> 01:09:01,211
This social experiment was
profoundly enlightening.

1359
01:09:01,479 --> 01:09:03,046
It expanded my worldview significantly.

1360
01:09:03,047 --> 01:09:06,417
I used to observe extreme
political polarization and wonder,

1361
01:09:06,418 --> 01:09:08,951
"What rational basis could
justify that stance?"

1362
01:09:08,952 --> 01:09:11,321
"Those people are impossible
to engage with."

1363
01:09:11,322 --> 01:09:13,524
That was my default assessment
before entering this house.

1364
01:09:13,525 --> 01:09:15,625
Living through this
proved that premise wrong.

1365
01:09:15,626 --> 01:09:18,228
Yet a degree of skepticism remains,

1366
01:09:18,229 --> 01:09:20,073
because an undeniable divide separates...

1367
01:09:20,097 --> 01:09:22,899
in-person engagement
from discourse mediated through screens.

1368
01:09:23,034 --> 01:09:28,304
Much of our broader social polarization
is manufactured and magnified...

1369
01:09:28,305 --> 01:09:32,175
in anonymous comment sections
and digital spaces.

1370
01:09:32,176 --> 01:09:34,377
Those populations rarely
have the incentive...

1371
01:09:34,378 --> 01:09:35,930
to sit across from one another...

1372
01:09:35,955 --> 01:09:37,857
and build mutual regard
the way we did here,

1373
01:09:37,882 --> 01:09:40,418
which makes systemic resolution
far harder to achieve.

1374
01:09:40,752 --> 01:09:44,955
(What does an ideology check mean to you?)

1375
01:09:45,156 --> 01:09:46,624
Exposing where everyone stands...

1376
01:09:46,791 --> 01:09:48,292
is inherently destabilizing.

1377
01:09:48,326 --> 01:09:50,962
Uncovering true motives demands
uncomfortable confrontation.

1378
01:09:51,295 --> 01:09:52,161
A bond?

1379
01:09:53,765 --> 01:09:55,333
It began as an intimidating label,

1380
01:09:55,833 --> 01:09:58,568
yet it ultimately functioned
as an adhesive that united us.

1381
01:09:58,870 --> 01:10:00,836
It compelled me to confront...

1382
01:10:00,837 --> 01:10:03,407
the actual utility of my own character.

1383
01:10:04,142 --> 01:10:05,610
Knowing someone's beliefs...

1384
01:10:05,877 --> 01:10:07,278
is not essential.

1385
01:10:09,981 --> 01:10:11,481
I've learned firsthand...

1386
01:10:12,016 --> 01:10:15,685
that you can have different beliefs
and still get along...

1387
01:10:15,710 --> 01:10:17,288
and live together.

1388
01:10:22,326 --> 01:10:26,439
Society continuously attempts
to polarize people...

1389
01:10:26,464 --> 01:10:29,266
by reducing complex realities
to binary yes-or-no choices.

1390
01:10:29,267 --> 01:10:32,269
As if existence offers only two options.

1391
01:10:33,604 --> 01:10:35,638
It flattens reality
into a rigid dichotomy...

1392
01:10:35,639 --> 01:10:37,517
specifically engineered
to generate conflict.

1393
01:10:37,542 --> 01:10:40,444
That's reductionist thinking at its worst.

1394
01:10:42,763 --> 01:10:45,349
Can a crude binary ever capture
the full scope of human utility?

1395
01:10:49,320 --> 01:10:51,055
Clearly, it cannot.

1396
01:10:51,056 --> 01:10:53,690
Human behavior and values are far more
nuanced than two options allow.

1397
01:10:53,691 --> 01:10:55,191
That is why direct
interpersonal engagement...

1398
01:10:55,192 --> 01:10:57,527
yields vastly more social value...

1399
01:10:57,528 --> 01:11:00,030
than relying on sweeping generalities.

1400
01:11:00,465 --> 01:11:03,300
Yet structured classification
serves a distinct function.

1401
01:11:03,468 --> 01:11:05,836
No individual fits a category seamlessly,

1402
01:11:05,837 --> 01:11:09,107
but sustaining an organized community...

1403
01:11:09,108 --> 01:11:14,178
requires some taxonomy
to parse collective diversity.

1404
01:11:14,871 --> 01:11:17,906
To fulfill our respective societal roles,

1405
01:11:18,149 --> 01:11:20,117
those structural frameworks provide...

1406
01:11:20,118 --> 01:11:23,453
essential baseline data
for social coordination.

1407
01:11:23,821 --> 01:11:25,820
So the mechanism is not without utility.

1408
01:11:25,821 --> 01:11:27,357
It provides meaningful
practical structure,

1409
01:11:27,459 --> 01:11:29,794
even if it remains an approximation
of the individual.

1410
01:11:31,929 --> 01:11:33,831
Furthermore, the visceral impact
is undeniable.

1411
01:11:33,832 --> 01:11:36,166
Encountering an ideology
as an abstract proposition...

1412
01:11:36,167 --> 01:11:40,169
or reading about it online is one thing.

1413
01:11:40,371 --> 01:11:42,572
It registers with entirely
different weight...

1414
01:11:42,573 --> 01:11:45,175
when expressed by a living person,

1415
01:11:45,176 --> 01:11:47,411
embodied in real-time actions and choices.

1416
01:11:47,412 --> 01:11:48,745
I fully agree.

1417
01:11:48,746 --> 01:11:49,646
Agreed.

1418
01:11:50,047 --> 01:11:52,683
That dynamic is precisely
what makes this so compelling.

1419
